/-
RSX LOWER — the reference lowering rsx → scm (hole 14, plan/PHASE1-BOUNDARY.md §14,
"lower: rsx -> scm (erasure, then defunctionalization, then fuel)"), its `#guard`
controls, and the per-construct adequacy statements.

Pipeline (each stage a total, executable, fueled definition; `Rsx.Lower.lowerF`):

  1. erasure       `Expr Nat → LExpr`   types, type formers and proofs become `□`
                                         (`LExpr.box`); binder types are dropped;
                                         transparent constants are unfolded (δ) and
                                         their bodies erased in the empty context.
  2. defunctionalization `LExpr → DExpr × List Code`  every λ becomes a first-order
                                         closure record `clo ℓ [captured]` and every
                                         application an `apply` node; `Code ℓ` is the
                                         λ's body over `arg :: captured` (flat closures).
  3. fuel          `run : List Code → Nat → …`  the first-order `apply` loop of the
                                         defunctionalized program, made total by fuel
                                         (fuel-out is `none`, never a value).
  4. emission      `DVal → BootExpr S G t`  the value is emitted at the requested scm
                                         type `t` (literal → `litI`, constructor →
                                         `inj ⟨ref⟩ (list fields)`, erased fields
                                         dropped); anything not representable at `t`
                                         is the refusing expression `unwrapSome noneE`
                                         (evaluates to `none`).

`Rsx.lower E : Expr Nat → BootExpr S [] t` is `lowerF E 0 defaultFuel t`.

Partial definitions (step 5, semantics/Rsx/Partial.rsd): erasure takes a global table
`gi`; a partial constant becomes `LExpr.glob i` / `DExpr.glob i`, resolved by `run` from
code entry `i` at one fuel tick per resolution, never inlined. The total lowering passes
`noGlobals`, so it never produces `glob` (`Rsx.Partial.lowerPF_nil`).

Sources (PREAMBLE item 7: ported, not invented):
- Erasure: P. Letouzey, "A New Extraction for Coq", TYPES 2002, LNCS 2646 — the `□`
  translation of the logical and type-level parts of CIC terms (the informative test:
  a term is erased when its type is an arity or its type's type is `Prop`).
  M. Sozeau, S. Boulier, Y. Forster, N. Tabareau, T. Winterhalter, "Coq Coq Correct!
  Verification of Type Checking and Erasure for Coq, in Coq", POPL 2020 — MetaCoq's
  `erase` (same test, `tBox`) and its correctness observation on first-order values,
  which is the shape of `Rsx.adequacyStatement` (Adequacy.rsd). Lean 4.14's own code generator
  makes the same cut: `src/library/compiler/erase_irrelevant.cpp` (types and proofs to
  the neutral value, binder types dropped) and, in the LCNF pipeline,
  `src/Lean/Compiler/LCNF/ToLCNF.lean` (`isProof` / type formers → `.erased`).
- Defunctionalization: J. C. Reynolds, "Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order
  Programming Languages", Proc. ACM Annual Conference 1972 (repr. HOSC 11(4), 1998),
  §8: each functional value becomes a record tagged by the λ it came from, carrying its
  free variables, and application becomes a call of one `apply` that dispatches on the
  tag. O. Danvy, L. R. Nielsen, "Defunctionalization at Work", PPDP 2001 (the
  correspondence with closure conversion; flat closures: the record holds exactly the
  λ's free variables, in first-occurrence order).
- Fuel: the totalization rsdc uses for every definition (a leading fuel `Nat`), and
  evalLF's own call-only fuel (N6c, `Residua/Bootstrap/Semantics.lean`).

Scope notes (facts, each witnessed by a control below; reports/rsxlower/GAPS.md):
- the statement Adequacy.rsd carried until 2026-11-18 (now `adequacyStatementWeak`) is
  provable for EVERY `lower`: its fuels are existential and both `eval … 0 …` and
  `scmValOf E 0 …` are `none` (`Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`). The official
  `Rsx.adequacyStatement` is now the strong form: rsx value fixed, scm fuel existential,
  lowering fuel eventual, and the scm value is `some w`.
- `BootExpr` is intrinsically typed with no recursive type and homogeneous lists, so a
  constructor value whose fields mix literals and constructors, or whose depth exceeds
  the requested type, has no scm term of that type; `valFits` names the representable
  values and the strong statement assumes it (control `gap_heterogeneous`).
- `scmValOf` keeps proof fields; erasure drops them (`relevantSpine` premise).
- a value of a Prop inductive (`True.intro : True`) is data for `DataTy` and `scmValOf`,
  and erasure maps it to `□`: the step-4 statement (`adequacyStatementNoRoot`) is false
  for this lowering (`lowerF_not_adequate_noRoot`); the statement on main assumes
  `irrelevant E n [] v = false` (session 7).
- literals beyond i64 refuse (`litI` range), while `scmValOf` returns `.int t`
  (control `gap_i64`).
- `lower` needs the environment `E` (δ bodies, constructor classes); the strong
  statement quantifies a lowering family `Rsx.Lowering S` that reads `E`, `n`, its fuel
  and the requested type, so `Rsx.lower E` is the family member at `n = 0`,
  `F = defaultFuel`.

Recipe (inner loop, one file plus its imports):

    { echo "import Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics";
      cat semantics/Rsx/Core.rsd semantics/Rsx/Norm.rsd
          semantics/Rsx/Adequacy.rsd semantics/Rsx/Lower.rsd; } > /tmp/rsx-lower.lean \
      && cd lean/rsd-cert && lake build Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics \
      && lake env lean /tmp/rsx-lower.lean

Expected: exit 0; every `#guard` passes; `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond
`propext`, `Quot.sound`.

closure_claim = 0.
-/

namespace Rsx
namespace Lower

open Residua.Bootstrap.IR Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics
open Residua.Bootstrap.EvalBootSeparators (inI64Range)

/-! ## Stage 1: erasure (Letouzey 2002; MetaCoq `erase`; Lean `erase_irrelevant`) -/

/-- erased λ-terms: de Bruijn, untyped; `box` is Letouzey's `□`. Constants left after
    δ are constructors (`ctor`) or rigid heads (`rigid`: axioms, opaques, recursors). -/
inductive LExpr : Type
  | bvar : Nat → LExpr
  | box : LExpr
  | lit : Nat → LExpr
  | ctor : Nat → LExpr
  | rigid : Nat → LExpr
  | app : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  | lam : LExpr → LExpr
  | letE : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  /-- a reference to global `i` of the program's partial definitions (Partial.rsd), resolved
      at run time, never inlined: its body may call itself. The total lowering has none. -/
  | glob : Nat → LExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/- The relevance test is `Rsx.irrelevant` (Adequacy.rsd): Letouzey's informative test
   read off the certified syntactic checker `inferT` — `e` is erased when its type is an
   arity or the type of its type is `Prop`; a term the checker cannot type is kept
   (erasure only ever errs toward keeping). It lives in Adequacy.rsd because the
   statement's proof-free side condition `relevantSpine` reads the same test. -/

def isCtor (E : ResolvedEnv) (r : Nat) : Bool :=
  match E.members r with
  | some m => decide (m.mclass = .constructorM)
  | none => false

/-- erasure, parametric in the relevance test `irr` (the reference instance is
    `irrelevant E n`; the controls plant a wrong one) and in the global table `gi`
    (`gi r = some i`: constant `r` is the `i`-th partial definition, erased to `glob i`
    and resolved at run time; the total lowering passes `noGlobals`). Fuel bounds depth
    plus δ. -/
def eraseWith (irr : LCtx → Expr Nat → Bool) (gi : Nat → Option Nat) (E : ResolvedEnv) :
    Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, _, .sort _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .pi _ _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, Γ, .bvar i => if irr Γ (.bvar i) then some .box else some (.bvar i)
  | f + 1, Γ, .const r ls =>
      if irr Γ (.const r ls) then some .box
      else
        match gi r with
        | some i => some (.glob i)
        | none =>
            match transparentBody E r ls with
            | some b => eraseWith irr gi E f [] b
            | none => some (if isCtor E r then .ctor r else .rigid r)
  | f + 1, Γ, .app g a =>
      if irr Γ (.app g a) then some .box
      else
        match eraseWith irr gi E f Γ g, eraseWith irr gi E f Γ a with
        | some g', some a' => some (.app g' a')
        | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, Γ, .lam A b =>
      if irr Γ (.lam A b) then some .box
      else (eraseWith irr gi E f (.assumption A :: Γ) b).map .lam
  | f + 1, Γ, .letE A v b =>
      if irr Γ (.letE A v b) then some .box
      else
        match eraseWith irr gi E f Γ v, eraseWith irr gi E f (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
        | some v', some b' => some (.letE v' b')
        | _, _ => none

/-- the empty global table: the total lowering has no partial definitions. -/
def noGlobals : Nat → Option Nat := fun _ => none

def erase (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) : Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr :=
  eraseWith (irrelevant E n) noGlobals E

/-! ## Stage 2: defunctionalization (Reynolds 1972 §8; Danvy–Nielsen 2001) -/

/-- the defunctionalized first-order language: `clo ℓ xs` builds the record of λ `ℓ`
    from the environment slots `xs`; `apply` is Reynolds' single dispatch. -/
inductive DExpr : Type
  | var : Nat → DExpr
  | box : DExpr
  | lit : Nat → DExpr
  | ctor : Nat → DExpr
  | rigid : Nat → DExpr
  | clo : Nat → List Nat → DExpr
  | apply : DExpr → DExpr → DExpr
  | letE : DExpr → DExpr → DExpr
  /-- global `ℓ`: run the closed code entry `ℓ` (a partial definition's body) in the empty
      environment; one fuel tick per resolution (the compiler-inserted fuel). -/
  | glob : Nat → DExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- the body of λ `ℓ`, over the environment `arg :: captured` (`ncap` captured slots). -/
structure Code where
  ncap : Nat
  body : DExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def addUniq (xs : List Nat) (x : Nat) : List Nat :=
  if xs.contains x then xs else xs ++ [x]

def unionL (xs ys : List Nat) : List Nat := ys.foldl addUniq xs

/-- free de Bruijn indices `≥ c`, shifted down by `c`, in first-occurrence order. -/
def freeVars (c : Nat) : LExpr → List Nat
  | .bvar i => if c ≤ i then [i - c] else []
  | .app f a => unionL (freeVars c f) (freeVars c a)
  | .lam b => freeVars (c + 1) b
  | .letE v b => unionL (freeVars c v) (freeVars (c + 1) b)
  | _ => []

def idxOf (x : Nat) : List Nat → Option Nat
  | [] => none
  | y :: ys => if x = y then some 0 else (idxOf x ys).map (· + 1)

/-- renaming under a `let`: slot 0 is the bound value. -/
def liftRen (ρ : Nat → Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => ρ i + 1

/-- renaming inside a λ body: slot 0 is the argument, slot `1 + k` the `k`-th captured
    variable; a variable not captured maps past the environment (lookup fails). -/
def capRen (fs : List Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => (idxOf i fs).getD fs.length + 1

/-- closure conversion + defunctionalization, parametric in the λ-body renaming `cr`
    (reference `capRen`). Labels are positions in the code table, inner λs first. -/
def convWith (cr : List Nat → Nat → Nat) (ρ : Nat → Nat) (code : List Code) :
    LExpr → DExpr × List Code
  | .bvar i => (.var (ρ i), code)
  | .box => (.box, code)
  | .lit k => (.lit k, code)
  | .ctor r => (.ctor r, code)
  | .rigid r => (.rigid r, code)
  | .glob i => (.glob i, code)
  | .app f a =>
      let p := convWith cr ρ code f
      let q := convWith cr ρ p.2 a
      (.apply p.1 q.1, q.2)
  | .lam b =>
      let fs := freeVars 1 b
      let p := convWith cr (cr fs) code b
      (.clo p.2.length (fs.map ρ), p.2 ++ [{ ncap := fs.length, body := p.1 }])
  | .letE v b =>
      let p := convWith cr ρ code v
      let q := convWith cr (liftRen ρ) p.2 b
      (.letE p.1 q.1, q.2)

def defunc (l : LExpr) : DExpr × List Code := convWith capRen id [] l

/-! ## Stage 3: fuel (the defunctionalized `apply` loop, totalized) -/

/-- first-order values: no meta-level functions anywhere. -/
inductive DVal : Type
  | box : DVal
  | lit : Nat → DVal
  | ctor : Nat → List DVal → DVal
  | rigid : Nat → List DVal → DVal
  | clo : Nat → List DVal → DVal

/-- the environment machine of the defunctionalized program, parametric in how `apply`
    binds the argument (reference: `a :: captured`). Fuel-out is `none`. -/
def runWith (bind : DVal → List DVal → List DVal) (code : List Code) :
    Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, env, .var i => env.get? i
  | _ + 1, _, .box => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, _, .ctor r => some (.ctor r [])
  | _ + 1, _, .rigid r => some (.rigid r [])
  | _ + 1, env, .clo l caps => (caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (.clo l)
  | f + 1, _, .glob l =>
      match code.get? l with
      | some c => runWith bind code f [] c.body
      | none => none
  | f + 1, env, .apply g a =>
      match runWith bind code f env g, runWith bind code f env a with
      | some (.clo l caps), some av =>
          match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code f (bind av caps) c.body
          | none => none
      | some (.ctor r args), some av => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
      | some (.rigid r args), some av => some (.rigid r (args ++ [av]))
      | some .box, some _ => some .box
      | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, env, .letE v b =>
      match runWith bind code f env v with
      | some vv => runWith bind code f (vv :: env) b
      | none => none

def bindArg (a : DVal) (caps : List DVal) : List DVal := a :: caps

def run (code : List Code) : Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal :=
  runWith bindArg code

/-! ## Stage 4: emission into the scm IR (`BootExpr`, evalLF's input) -/

/-- the refusing scm term at every type: `unwrapSome noneE` evaluates to `none`. -/
def refuse {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t : BootTy} : BootExpr S G t := .unwrapSome .noneE

def listOf {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {τ : BootTy} :
    List (BootExpr S G τ) → BootExpr S G (.list τ)
  | [] => .emptyList
  | e :: es => .listAppend (.listSingleton e) (listOf es)

/-- constructor fields after erasure: `□` fields (parameters, proofs) are dropped, as
    Lean's constructor layout drops irrelevant fields. -/
def relevantArgs (args : List DVal) : List DVal :=
  args.filter (fun v => match v with | .box => false | _ => true)

/-- emission at the requested type, parametric in the field selection (reference
    `relevantArgs`). Convention (the one `scmValOf` fixes): literal `k` ↦ `.int k`;
    constructor `r` ↦ summand `r` of a sum whose summand `r` is `list τ`. -/
def emitWith (fields : List DVal → List DVal) {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} :
    Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S G t
  | 0, _, _ => refuse
  | _ + 1, .i64, .lit k =>
      if inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) then .litI (Int.ofNat k) else refuse
  | f + 1, .sum ts, .ctor r args =>
      if h : r < ts.length then
        match hτ : ts.get ⟨r, h⟩ with
        | .list τ =>
            .inj ⟨r, h⟩ (cast (congrArg (BootExpr S G) hτ.symm)
              (listOf ((fields args).map (emitWith fields f τ))))
        | _ => refuse
      else refuse
  | _ + 1, _, _ => refuse

def emit {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} : Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S G t :=
  emitWith relevantArgs

/-! ## The lowering -/

/-- the four stages composed; every stage is a parameter so a planted mutant is the
    same composition with one stage replaced. -/
def pipeline {S : SigTable} (eraseS : Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr)
    (defuncS : LExpr → DExpr × List Code)
    (runS : List Code → Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal)
    (emitS : Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S [] t)
    (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr S [] t :=
  match eraseS F [] e with
  | none => refuse
  | some l =>
      match runS (defuncS l).2 F [] (defuncS l).1 with
      | some v => emitS F t v
      | none => refuse

/-- the reference lowering at universe context `n` and fuel `F`. -/
def lowerF (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) {S : SigTable} (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) :
    BootExpr S [] t :=
  pipeline (erase E n) defunc run emit F t e

def defaultFuel : Nat := 10000

end Lower

/-- `Rsx.lower`: the reference lowering rsx → scm with the brief's signature
    (`E` supplies δ bodies and constructor classes). -/
def lower (E : ResolvedEnv) {S : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.SigTable} {t : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.BootTy}
    (e : Expr Nat) : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.BootExpr S [] t :=
  Lower.lowerF E 0 Lower.defaultFuel t e

namespace Lower

open Residua.Bootstrap.IR Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics
open Residua.Bootstrap.EvalBootSeparators (inI64Range)

/-! ## Adequacy statements

The hole-14 statement is `Rsx.adequacyStatement` (Adequacy.rsd, strong form since
2026-11-18): rsx value `w` fixed, scm fuel existential, lowering fuel eventual. Its
side conditions `relevantSpine`, `valFits` and the vacuity control for the weak form
(`Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`) live there too. The reference instance is the family
`fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F t e`; `Rsx.lower E` is its member at `n = 0`,
`F = defaultFuel`. -/

/-- the old (weak) form for `Rsx.lower`: it holds, and says nothing (every lowering
    meets it, `Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`). -/
theorem lower_adequacyStatementWeak (E : ResolvedEnv) {S : SigTable} {t : BootTy}
    (progs : Programs S S) : adequacyStatementWeak (Rsx.lower E (S := S) (t := t)) progs :=
  adequacyStatement_vacuous _ progs

/-- structural erasure finishes: `erase` returns a term at some fuel.
    `whnfFuel` (Core.rsd, frozen) is call-by-name, so `norm` can discard a relevant
    argument; `erase` traverses it. A transparent `loop := loop` in that argument has a
    `norm` and no finite erasure (`lowerF_not_adequate_divArg`). MetaCoq's erasure
    correctness (Sozeau et al., POPL 2020, §4) assumes the source is defined, which
    here is this premise. -/
def Erasable (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∃ (F : Nat) (l : LExpr), erase E n F [] e = some l

theorem erasable_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n k : Nat) : Erasable E n (.lit k) :=
  ⟨1, .lit k, rfl⟩

/-- adequacy of `Rsx.Lower.lowerF` at one closed term (the body of
    `Rsx.Lower.adequacyClosed` at `e`). -/
def Good {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
    Erasable E n e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w

/-- hole-14 statement for the reference family, with the erasability premise.
    `Rsx.adequacyStatement` (Adequacy.rsd) is the previous form; the reference
    lowering refutes it (`lowerF_not_adequate_divArg`). -/
def adequacyClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf fv : Nat) (e T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
    Erasable E n e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w

/-! ### One statement per `Expr` constructor (8/8). Proved: bvar, sort, pi, lam, lit.
    Stated (Prop objects, no `sorry`): const (δ and constructor heads), app (β and
    constructor spines), letE (ζ). The const case is split below: its head half
    (`adeqConstHead`, no transparent body) is proved; its δ half `AdeqConstDelta` is open. -/

def AdeqBvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n i, Good progs E n (.bvar i)
def AdeqSort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n l, Good progs E n (.sort l)
def AdeqConst {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls, Good progs E n (.const r ls)
def AdeqApp {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n f a, Good progs E n (.app f a)
def AdeqLam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A b, Good progs E n (.lam A b)
def AdeqPi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A B, Good progs E n (.pi A B)
def AdeqLetE {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A v b, Good progs E n (.letE A v b)
def AdeqLit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n k, Good progs E n (.lit k)

/-- the eight per-construct statements together give `adequacyClosed` for the
    reference family `Rsx.Lower.lowerF` (case split on the term). -/
theorem adequacy_of_constructs {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (hb : AdeqBvar progs) (hs : AdeqSort progs) (hc : AdeqConst progs)
    (ha : AdeqApp progs) (hl : AdeqLam progs) (hp : AdeqPi progs)
    (hz : AdeqLetE progs) (hn : AdeqLit progs) :
    adequacyClosed (S := S) progs := by
  intro E n lf fv e T v t w
  cases e with
  | bvar i => exact hb E n i lf fv T v t w
  | sort l => exact hs E n l lf fv T v t w
  | const r ls => exact hc E n r ls lf fv T v t w
  | app f a => exact ha E n f a lf fv T v t w
  | lam A b => exact hl E n A b lf fv T v t w
  | pi A B => exact hp E n A B lf fv T v t w
  | letE A x b => exact hz E n A x b lf fv T v t w
  | lit k => exact hn E n k lf fv T v t w

/-! ### The direct cases -/

theorem norm_bvar_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf i : Nat} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.bvar i) = some v) : v = .bvar i := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_sort_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {l : Level} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.sort l) = some v) : v = .sort l := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.sort l) = some (.sort l) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_lit_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf k : Nat} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.lit k) = some v) : v = .lit k := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_pi_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {A B v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.pi A B) = some v) : ∃ A' B', v = .pi A' B' := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.pi A B) =
          (match norm E (j + 1) A, norm E (j + 1) B with
           | some A', some B' => some (.pi A' B')
           | _, _ => none) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      split at h
      · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
      · exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem norm_lam_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {A b v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.lam A b) = some v) : ∃ A' b', v = .lam A' b' := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.lam A b) =
          (match norm E (j + 1) A, norm E (j + 1) b with
           | some A', some b' => some (.lam A' b')
           | _, _ => none) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      split at h
      · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
      · exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem scmValOf_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv i : Nat) : scmValOf E fv (.bvar i) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (l : Level) :
    scmValOf E fv (.sort l) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    scmValOf E fv (.pi A B) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    scmValOf E fv (.lam A b) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

/- A constant that is not a constructor is not data. `scmValOf` returns
   `none` for an axiom, an opaque, an inductive, a recursor, or a missing
   member. -/
theorem scmValOf_const_not_ctor (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv c : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnot : ∀ m, E.members c = some m → ¬ m.mclass = .constructorM) :
    scmValOf E fv (.const c ls) = none := by
  cases fv with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ _ =>
    cases hm : E.members c with
    | none => simp [scmValOf, appsSpine, hm]
    | some m =>
      have hne := hnot m hm
      simp [scmValOf, appsSpine, hm, hne]

theorem adeqBvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqBvar progs := by
  intro E n i lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_bvar_val hn, scmValOf_bvar] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqSort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqSort progs := by
  intro E n l lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_sort_val hn, scmValOf_sort] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqPi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqPi progs := by
  intro E n A B lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_pi_val hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_pi] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqLam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqLam progs := by
  intro E n A b lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_lam_val hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_lam] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-- the lowering of a literal, by computation through the four stages, at every
    positive lowering fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n k F : Nat) {S : SigTable} :
    lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k) =
      (if inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) then .litI (Int.ofNat k) else refuse) := rfl

theorem eval_litI {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (x : Int)
    (hx : inI64Range x = true) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 [] (BootExpr.litI (S := S) (G := []) x)
      = some (.int x) := by
  simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, hx]

theorem adeqLit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqLit progs := by
  intro E n k lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  rw [norm_lit_val hn] at hs
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
      have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
      rw [hs2] at hs
      cases hs
      cases t
      case i64 =>
          have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
          refine ⟨1, fun F hF => ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
          obtain ⟨F', rfl⟩ : ∃ F', F = F' + 1 := ⟨F - 1, by omega⟩
          rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
          exact eval_litI progs _ hk
      all_goals cases hf

/-- positive control at the concrete term on which Adequacy.rsd refutes the two mutants
    (`lit 0 : N` in `adqEnv`, value `.int 0`, scm type `i64`): the reference family
    meets the strong statement there. -/
theorem lit0_good {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F → ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
      (lowerF adqEnv 0 F (S := S) .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 0) :=
  adeqLit progs adqEnv 0 0 2 1 _ (.lit 0) .i64 (.int 0) adqBodiesTyped adqLit0Infer adqLit0Data adqLit0Norm
    adqLit0Val adqLit0Rel adqLit0Root adqLit0Fits adqLit0VInfer (erasable_lit _ _ _)

/-! ### Fuel monotonicity of the erase and run stages

The strong statement's lowering fuel is eventual (`∀ F ≥ F₀`); these lemmas are what the
open cases (const, app, letE) use to move a successful stage result to a larger fuel. -/

theorem eraseWith_mono (irr : LCtx → Expr Nat → Bool) (gi : Nat → Option Nat)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) :
    ∀ (F F' : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr), F ≤ F' →
      eraseWith irr gi E F Γ e = some l → eraseWith irr gi E F' Γ e = some l := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero => intro F' Γ e l _ h; exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
    intro F' Γ e l hF h
    obtain ⟨F'', rfl⟩ : ∃ F'', F' = F'' + 1 := ⟨F' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hF' : F ≤ F'' := by omega
    cases e with
    | sort _ => exact h
    | pi _ _ => exact h
    | lit _ => exact h
    | bvar _ => exact h
    | const r ls =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.const r ls)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hg : gi r with
          | some i => rw [hg] at h; exact h
          | none =>
            rw [hg] at h
            cases hb : transparentBody E r ls with
            | none => rw [hb] at h; exact h
            | some b => rw [hb] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | app g a =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.app g a)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hg : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ g with
          | none => rw [hg] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some g' =>
            cases ha : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ a with
            | none => rw [hg, ha] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some a' =>
              rw [hg, ha] at h
              rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hg, ih _ _ _ _ hF' ha]
              exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | lam A b =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.lam A b)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hb : eraseWith irr gi E F (.assumption A :: Γ) b with
          | none => rw [hb] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some b' => rw [hb] at h; rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hb]; exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | letE A v b =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.letE A v b)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hv : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ v with
          | none => rw [hv] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some v' =>
            cases hb : eraseWith irr gi E F (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
            | none => rw [hv, hb] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some b' =>
              rw [hv, hb] at h
              rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hv, ih _ _ _ _ hF' hb]
              exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h

theorem erase_mono (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F F' : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr)
    (hF : F ≤ F') (h : erase E n F Γ e = some l) : erase E n F' Γ e = some l :=
  eraseWith_mono (irrelevant E n) noGlobals E F F' Γ e l hF h

/- A transparent constant erases as its body, one fuel earlier, in the empty
   context. Letouzey TYPES 2002 unfolds δ before the informative test of the
   body; Sozeau et al. POPL 2020 §4 erase a constant as the erasure of its body.
   `noGlobals` sends the constant nowhere, so this is not a `glob`. -/
theorem erase_const_delta (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b) :
    erase E n (F + 1) [] (.const r ls) = erase E n F [] b := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hb]

/- A relevant application erases as the application of the two erasures,
   one fuel earlier. Letouzey TYPES 2002 keeps an informative application.
   The AdeqApp relevant branch rewrites with this. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem erase_app_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (g a : Expr Nat)
    (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.app g a) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.app g a) =
      match erase E n F Γ g, erase E n F Γ a with
      | some g', some a' => some (.app g' a')
      | _, _ => none := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- A relevant lambda erases as the lambda of its body, domain dropped,
   one fuel earlier, under the assumption. Not AdeqLam: that one is
   already proved, because a lambda is not data. -/
theorem erase_lam_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (A b : Expr Nat)
    (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.lam A b) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.lam A b) =
      (erase E n F (.assumption A :: Γ) b).map .lam := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- A relevant let erases as the let of the two erasures, one fuel earlier.
   The body is erased under the let binding. The AdeqLetE relevant branch
   rewrites with this. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem erase_let_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx)
    (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.letE A v b) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.letE A v b) =
      match erase E n F Γ v, erase E n F (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
      | some v', some b' => some (.letE v' b')
      | _, _ => none := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- `whnfFuel` unfolds the same δ, and `foldApps body []` is the body. -/
theorem whnf_const_delta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = whnfFuel E k b := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, hb]

/- If the body normalizes at fuel `k + 1`, the constant normalizes to that
   value at fuel `k + 2`. `whnf_const_delta` makes the two heads the same
   `whnf`, and `norm_mono` moves the body's value up one fuel, where both
   `norm`s normalize the same subterms. The unconditional equality, with no
   success hypothesis on the body, is the false one named below.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_of_body (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body v : Expr Nat) (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) body = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.const r ls) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k body with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_const_delta E k r ls body ht]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) body = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k body w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.const r ls) = norm E (k + 2) body := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) body v hn

/- A literal body has no subterm for `norm` to revisit, so the fuel shift is
   only the one `whnf_const_delta` performs. One fuel makes `whnfFuel` return
   the literal. The general equality `norm` of the constant at `k + 2` equals
   `norm` of an arbitrary body at `k + 1` is false: the constant normalizes
   subterms at fuel `k + 1` and the body at fuel `k`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r n : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit n)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.lit n) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit n) = some (.lit n) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.lit n) hb, hw]

/- Any successful `norm` of that constant is the literal. Fuels 0, 1 and 2
   return `none` (`whnfFuel` of the literal needs one fuel, and `norm` spends
   one more). -/
theorem norm_const_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r n : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit n))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .lit n := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.lit n) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_lit E j r n ls hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A sort body is the same canonical head. `scmValOf` of a sort is `none`,
   so this case of δ is vacuous once `norm` returns the sort. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.sort u) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.sort u) = some (.sort u) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.sort u) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_sort_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .sort u := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.sort u) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_sort E j r ls u hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A bound variable is a canonical head. `scmValOf` of it is `none`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.bvar i) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.bvar i) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_bvar_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .bvar i := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.bvar i) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_bvar E j r i ls hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A Π body is not rewritten away by `whnfFuel`. A successful `norm` of the
   constant is a Π; its subterms are normalized one fuel later than `norm`
   of the body, so the two `norm`s are not equal. -/
theorem norm_const_pi_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (A B : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.pi A B))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : ∃ A' B', v = .pi A' B' := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.pi A B) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.pi A B) = some (.pi A B) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
        have h2 : norm E (j + 3) (.const r ls) =
            (match norm E (j + 2) A, norm E (j + 2) B with
             | some A', some B' => some (.pi A' B')
             | _, _ => none) := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnf_const_delta E (j + 1) r ls (.pi A B) hb, hw]
          rfl
        rw [h2] at hn
        split at hn
        · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩
        · exact Option.noConfusion hn

/- A λ body is the same shape as a Π body. -/
theorem norm_const_lam_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (A b : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lam A b))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : ∃ A' b', v = .lam A' b' := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.lam A b) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.lam A b) = some (.lam A b) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
        have h2 : norm E (j + 3) (.const r ls) =
            (match norm E (j + 2) A, norm E (j + 2) b with
             | some A', some b' => some (.lam A' b')
             | _, _ => none) := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnf_const_delta E (j + 1) r ls (.lam A b) hb, hw]
          rfl
        rw [h2] at hn
        split at hn
        · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩
        · exact Option.noConfusion hn

/- A constructor head has no transparent body, so `norm` does not open it.
   The fuel shift is only the one `whnf_const_delta` performs. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_ctor (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.const c lsc) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const c lsc) = some (.const c lsc) := by
    change (match transparentBody E c lsc with
      | some body => whnfFuel E k (foldApps body [])
      | none => some (.const c lsc)) = some (.const c lsc)
    rw [hnone]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.const c lsc) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_ctor_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .const c lsc := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.const c lsc) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_ctor E j r c ls lsc hb hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A constructor applied to one literal. The head is rigid, so `whnfFuel`
   returns the application, and `norm` normalizes the literal argument.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_app_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hwb : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) hb, hwb]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_const_app_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_app_lit E j r c nlit ls lsc hb hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- One more transparent constant in front of a literal. Each δ spends one
   fuel in `whnfFuel`, and `norm` spends one more, so the literal appears
   at fuel `k + 4`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_lit_via (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r m nlit : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit nlit)) :
    norm E (k + 4) (.const r ls) = some (.lit nlit) := by
  have hl : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.const m lsm) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) m lsm (.lit nlit) hm, hl]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 2) r ls (.const m lsm) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_lit_via_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r m nlit : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit nlit))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .lit nlit := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.const m lsm) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ lf =>
        cases lf with
        | zero =>
          have hw := whnf_const_delta E 1 r ls (.const m lsm) hb
          have hw2 := whnf_const_delta E 0 m lsm (.lit nlit) hm
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw2
          rw [hw2] at hw
          rw [hw] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
        | succ j =>
          rw [norm_const_delta_lit_via E j r m nlit ls lsm hb hm] at hn
          exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

theorem runWith_mono (bind : DVal → List DVal → List DVal) (code : List Code) :
    ∀ (F F' : Nat) (env : List DVal) (d : DExpr) (v : DVal), F ≤ F' →
      runWith bind code F env d = some v → runWith bind code F' env d = some v := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero => intro F' env d v _ h; exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
    intro F' env d v hF h
    obtain ⟨F'', rfl⟩ : ∃ F'', F' = F'' + 1 := ⟨F' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hF' : F ≤ F'' := by omega
    cases d with
    | var _ => exact h
    | box => exact h
    | lit _ => exact h
    | ctor _ => exact h
    | rigid _ => exact h
    | clo _ _ => exact h
    | glob l =>
        change (match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code F [] c.body
          | none => none) = some v at h
        change (match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code F'' [] c.body
          | none => none) = some v
        cases hc : code.get? l with
        | none => rw [hc] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some c => rw [hc] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
    | apply g a =>
        simp only [runWith] at h ⊢
        cases hg : runWith bind code F env g with
        | none => rw [hg] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some gv =>
          cases ha : runWith bind code F env a with
          | none => rw [hg, ha] at h; cases gv <;> exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some av =>
            rw [hg, ha] at h
            rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hg, ih _ _ _ _ hF' ha]
            cases gv with
            | clo l caps =>
                change (match code.get? l with
                  | some c => runWith bind code F (bind av caps) c.body
                  | none => none) = some v at h
                change (match code.get? l with
                  | some c => runWith bind code F'' (bind av caps) c.body
                  | none => none) = some v
                cases hc : code.get? l with
                | none => rw [hc] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
                | some c => rw [hc] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
            | _ => exact h
    | letE x b =>
        simp only [runWith] at h ⊢
        cases hx : runWith bind code F env x with
        | none => rw [hx] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some xv => rw [hx] at h; rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hx]; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h

theorem run_mono (code : List Code) (F F' : Nat) (env : List DVal) (d : DExpr) (v : DVal)
    (hF : F ≤ F') (h : run code F env d = some v) : run code F' env d = some v :=
  runWith_mono bindArg code F F' env d v hF h

/-! ### Emission and the whole lowering keep a successful result at every larger fuel

`emitWith` fails only by emitting `refuse` where its fuel runs out, and every node it
emits is evaluated (it emits no branching construct), so if evalLF of the emitted term
gives a value, the term emitted at a larger fuel gives the same value
(`emitWith_evalStable`). With `erase_mono` and `run_mono` this gives
`lowerF_evalStable`: a value evalLF gets from the lowering at fuel `F` it gets, at the
same scm fuel, from the lowering at every `F' ≥ F`. So for the reference family the
statement's eventual lowering fuel follows from a single one
(`lowerF_eventual_of_exists`, `good_of_exists`), and `FuelStable` separates it from a
lowering whose output depends on the fuel (`fuelParity_not_fuelStable`). -/

theorem eval_refuse_ne {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (w : Val) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (refuse (S := S) (G := G) (t := t))
      ≠ some w := by
  intro h
  have h2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
      (refuse (S := S) (G := G) (t := t)) = none := eval_refuse progs lf env
  rw [h2] at h
  exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem eval_cast_eq {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t t' : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (h : t = t') (x : BootExpr S G t) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (cast (congrArg (BootExpr S G) h) x)
      = Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env x := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- a list of emitted elements: if every element's value is kept when its emitter is
    replaced, the list's value is kept. -/
theorem eval_listOf_map {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {τ : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (g g' : DVal → BootExpr S G τ) :
    ∀ (xs : List DVal) (w : Val),
      (∀ x, x ∈ xs → ∀ u, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (g x) = some u →
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (g' x) = some u) →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (listOf (xs.map g)) = some w →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (listOf (xs.map g')) = some w
  | [], _, _, h => h
  | x :: xs, w, hg, h => by
    cases lf with
    | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
    | succ m =>
      change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
        (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g x)) (listOf (xs.map g))) = some w at h
      change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
        (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g' x)) (listOf (xs.map g'))) = some w
      simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h ⊢
      cases hx : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env (g x) with
      | none => rw [hx] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
      | some xv =>
        cases hr : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
            (listOf (xs.map g)) with
        | none => rw [hx, hr] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some rv =>
          rw [hg x (List.mem_cons_self x xs) xv hx,
            eval_listOf_map progs (m + 1) env g g' xs rv
              (fun y hy => hg y (List.mem_cons_of_mem x hy)) hr]
          rw [hx, hr] at h
          exact h

theorem emitWith_evalStable (fields : List DVal → List DVal) {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx}
    (progs : Programs S S) (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) :
    ∀ (f f' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (v : DVal) (w : Val), f ≤ f' →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
        (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f t v) = some w →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
        (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f' t v) = some w := by
  intro f
  induction f with
  | zero =>
    intro f' t v w _ h
    have h0 : emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) 0 t v = refuse := by
      cases t <;> cases v <;> rfl
    rw [h0] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
  | succ f ih =>
    intro f' t v w hf h
    obtain ⟨f'', rfl⟩ : ∃ f'', f' = f'' + 1 := ⟨f' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hf' : f ≤ f'' := by omega
    cases t <;> cases v <;> try exact h
    rename_i ts r args
    simp only [emitWith] at h ⊢
    by_cases hr : r < ts.length
    · rw [dif_pos hr] at h ⊢
      split
      · rename_i τ' hτ'
        split at h
        · rename_i τ hτ
          have hττ : τ' = τ := by rw [hτ] at hτ'; exact (BootTy.list.inj hτ').symm
          subst hττ
          cases lf with
          | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | succ m =>
            simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h ⊢
            rw [eval_cast_eq progs (m + 1) env hτ.symm] at h ⊢
            cases hl : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
                (listOf ((fields args).map (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f τ'))) with
            | none => rw [hl] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some lv =>
              rw [eval_listOf_map progs (m + 1) env _ _ (fields args) lv
                (fun x _ u hu => ih f'' τ' x u hf' hu) hl]
              rw [hl] at h
              exact h
        · exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
      · split at h
        · rename_i hn τ hτ
          exact absurd hτ (hn τ)
        · exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
    · rw [dif_neg hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)

/- Eval of the constant at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the body at fuel `F`, when the
   constant is relevant. Erasure agrees by `erase_const_delta`; `run` and `emit`
   keep a value at the larger fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_const_delta_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n F r lf : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b)
    (h : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t b)
      = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.const r ls)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline at h ⊢
  cases he : erase E n F [] b with
  | none =>
    simp only [he] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
  | some l =>
    simp only [he] at h
    have he' := (erase_const_delta E n F r ls b hirr hb).trans he
    simp only [he']
    cases hr : run (defunc l).2 F [] (defunc l).1 with
    | none =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
    | some v =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      have hr' := run_mono (defunc l).2 F (F + 1) [] (defunc l).1 v (Nat.le_succ F) hr
      simp only [hr']
      exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t v w (Nat.le_succ F) h

theorem lowerF_evalStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n F F' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (lf : Nat) (w : Val) (hF : F ≤ F')
    (h : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
      = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F' (S := S) t e)
      = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline at h ⊢
  cases he : erase E n F [] e with
  | none =>
    simp only [he] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
  | some l =>
    simp only [he] at h
    simp only [erase_mono E n F F' [] e l hF he]
    cases hr : run (defunc l).2 F [] (defunc l).1 with
    | none =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
    | some v =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      simp only [run_mono _ F F' [] _ v hF hr]
      exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F F' t v w hF h

/-- for the reference family, one lowering fuel that works gives the statement's
    eventual one. -/
theorem lowerF_eventual_of_exists {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (w : Val)
    (h : ∃ F lf, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
      = some w) :
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F → ∃ lf,
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) = some w := by
  obtain ⟨F, lf, h⟩ := h
  exact ⟨F, fun F' hF => ⟨lf, lowerF_evalStable progs E n F F' t e lf w hF h⟩⟩

/-- `Good` (the per-term body of the statement) from a single lowering fuel: the form the
    open const/app/letE cases can be proved in. -/
theorem good_of_exists {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat)
    (h : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      BodiesTyped E n →
      inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
      norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      Erasable E n e →
      ∃ F lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w) :
    Good progs E n e := by
  intro lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h7 h6 h8 h9
  exact lowerF_eventual_of_exists progs E n t e w (h lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h7 h6 h8 h9)

/- A transparent constant whose body is a literal denotes that literal.
   This is the literal slice of `AdeqConstDelta`, not the whole statement:
   `Good`'s irrelevance premise is about the value, and the value is the
   literal, so relevance of the constant is a separate hypothesis. -/
theorem good_const_delta_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r k : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit k))
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_lit_val E lf r k ls hb hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n (0 + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k)) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := by
        rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat k) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 r 1 ls (.lit k) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirr hb hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- The same literal, behind one more transparent constant. Each constant
   needs its own relevance hypothesis. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_lit_via {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r m k : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit k))
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hirrm : irrelevant E n [] (.const m lsm) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_lit_via_val E lf r m k ls lsm hb hm hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ q =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
      have hlit : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n (0 + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k)) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := by
        rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat k) hk
      have hmid := lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 m 1 lsm (.lit k) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirrm hm hlit
      exact ⟨3, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 2 r 1 ls (.const m lsm) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirr hb hmid⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A transparent constant whose body is a sort has no scm value.
   `AdeqConstDelta` still quantifies over every body. -/
theorem good_const_delta_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_const_sort_val E lf r ls u hb hn, scmValOf_sort] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/- A transparent constant whose body is a bound variable, a Π, or a λ has
   no scm value. None of these is `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_bvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_const_bvar_val E lf r i ls hb hn, scmValOf_bvar] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem good_const_delta_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.pi A B)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_const_pi_val E lf r ls A B hb hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_pi] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem good_const_delta_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (A b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lam A b)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_const_lam_val E lf r ls A b hb hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_lam] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-! ### The const case, split: heads proved, δ stated

`AdeqConst` follows from `AdeqConstHead` (a constant with no transparent body:
constructor, axiom, opaque, recursor; `norm` leaves it, erasure keeps it as `ctor`/`rigid`)
and `AdeqConstDelta` (a transparent constant: its value is its unfolded body's, so the case
needs the erasure/run simulation the app and letE cases need; stated, open). -/

def AdeqConstHead {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls, transparentBody E r ls = none → Good progs E n (.const r ls)
def AdeqConstDelta {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls b, transparentBody E r ls = some b → Good progs E n (.const r ls)

theorem adeqConst_of_split {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (hh : AdeqConstHead progs) (hd : AdeqConstDelta progs) : AdeqConst progs := by
  intro E n r ls
  cases hb : transparentBody E r ls with
  | none => exact hh E n r ls hb
  | some b => exact hd E n r ls b hb

theorem norm_const_head {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = none) (h : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) :
    v = .const r ls := by
  have key : ∀ k, whnfFuel E k (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) →
      norm E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
    intro k hk
    rw [norm, hk]
    try rfl
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
        change (match transparentBody E r ls with
          | some body => whnfFuel E j (foldApps body [])
          | none => some (.const r ls)) = some (.const r ls)
        rw [hb]
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := key (j + 1) hw
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem list_get?_some {α : Type} : ∀ (ts : List α) (r : Nat) (x : α),
    ts.get? r = some x → ∃ h : r < ts.length, ts.get ⟨r, h⟩ = x
  | [], _, _, h => Option.noConfusion h
  | _ :: _, 0, _, h => ⟨Nat.zero_lt_succ _, Option.some.inj h⟩
  | _ :: ys, k + 1, x, h =>
      let ⟨hk, he⟩ := list_get?_some ys k x h
      ⟨Nat.succ_lt_succ hk, he⟩

/-- the head case: a constant with no transparent body whose value is data is a nullary
    constructor, erased to `ctor r`, run to `ctor r []`, emitted as summand `r` with no
    fields; evalLF gives `.inj r (.list [])` at scm fuel 1, from lowering fuel 1 on. -/
theorem adeqConstHead {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqConstHead progs := by
  intro E n r ls hb lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hroot hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_head hb hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs' : (match E.members r with
        | some mm => if mm.mclass = .constructorM then some (Val.inj r (.list [])) else none
        | none => none) = some w := hs
    cases hm : E.members r with
    | none => rw [hm] at hs'; exact Option.noConfusion hs'
    | some mm =>
      rw [hm] at hs'
      by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
      · simp [hc] at hs'
        subst hs'
        cases t with
        | sum ts =>
          have hf' : (match ts.get? r with
              | some (.list τ) => ([] : List Val).all (valFits m τ)
              | _ => false) = true := hf
          split at hf'
          · rename_i τ hg
            obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
            have hctor : isCtor E r = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hc]
            refine ⟨1, fun F hF => ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
            obtain ⟨F', rfl⟩ : ∃ F', F = F' + 1 := ⟨F - 1, by omega⟩
            have he : erase E n (F' + 1) [] (.const r ls) = some (.ctor r) := by
              simp only [erase, eraseWith, hroot, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hb,
                hctor, if_true]
            have hlow : lowerF E n (F' + 1) (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const r ls) =
                emit (F' + 1) (.sum ts) (.ctor r []) := by
              unfold lowerF pipeline
              rw [he]
              rfl
            rw [hlow]
            simp only [emit, emitWith]
            rw [dif_pos hlt]
            split
            · rename_i τ' hτ'
              simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
              rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
              simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
            · rename_i hne
              exact absurd hget (hne τ)
          · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
        | _ => cases hf
      · simp [hc] at hs'

/- A transparent constant whose body is a constructor head denotes that
   constructor. Relevance of the constant is a hypothesis: `Good`'s
   irrelevance premise is about the value. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_ctor {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_ctor_val E lf r c ls lsc hb hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs' : (match E.members c with
        | some mm => if mm.mclass = .constructorM then some (Val.inj c (.list [])) else none
        | none => none) = some w := hs
    cases hm : E.members c with
    | none => rw [hm] at hs'; exact Option.noConfusion hs'
    | some mm =>
      rw [hm] at hs'
      by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
      · simp [hcm] at hs'
        subst hs'
        cases t with
        | sum ts =>
          have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
              | some (.list τ) => ([] : List Val).all (valFits m τ)
              | _ => false) = true := hf
          split at hf'
          · rename_i τ hg
            obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts c _ hg
            have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
            have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                (lowerF E n 1 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const c lsc)) =
                some (.inj c (.list [])) := by
              have he : erase E n 1 [] (.const c lsc) = some (.ctor c) := by
                simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals,
                  hnone, hctor, if_true]
              have hlow : lowerF E n 1 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const c lsc) =
                  emit 1 (.sum ts) (.ctor c []) := by
                unfold lowerF pipeline
                rw [he]
                rfl
              rw [hlow]
              simp only [emit, emitWith]
              rw [dif_pos hlt]
              split
              · rename_i τ' hτ'
                simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
                rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
                simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
              · rename_i hne
                exact absurd hget (hne τ)
            exact ⟨2, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 r 1 ls (.const c lsc)
              (.sum ts) (.inj c (.list [])) hirr hb hbody⟩
          · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
        | _ => cases hf
      · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- Emit a constructor whose one field is a literal, at lowering fuel 2
   (the field emitter needs one fuel) and scm fuel 1. -/
theorem eval_emit_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (nlit r : Nat)
    (ts : List BootTy) (hg : ts.get? r = some (.list .i64))
    (hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor r [.lit nlit])) =
      some (.inj r (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
  obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
  simp only [emit, emitWith]
  rw [dif_pos hlt]
  split
  · rename_i τ' hτ'
    have hτi : τ' = .i64 :=
      BootTy.list.inj (hτ'.symm.trans hget)
    subst hτi
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
    rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf, emitWith]
    rw [if_pos hk]
    simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, hk]
    have hk' : inI64Range (↑nlit) = true := hk
    rw [if_pos hk']
    rfl
  · rename_i hne
    exact absurd hget (hne .i64)

/- A transparent constant whose body is a constructor applied to one literal.
   The head stays a constructor (`hnone`). Relevance of the outer constant is
   what `lowerF_const_delta_eval` reads; relevance of the head is what erasure
   of that head reads. The value's relevance is `Good`'s own premise.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem good_const_delta_app_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_app_lit_val E lf r c nlit ls lsc hb hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) => ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have he : erase E n 2 [] (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                exact ⟨3, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 2 r 1 ls
                  (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) (.sum ts)
                  (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) hirr hb hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- The application itself, not a constant in front of it. The head is rigid,
   so `whnfFuel` returns the application and `norm` normalizes the literal.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_app_ctor_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hwb : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [hwb]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_app_ctor_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hwb : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
            some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
        have hlit0 : norm E 1 (.lit nlit) = none := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hwb] at hn
        have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
            (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
          simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
        simp only [hsp] at hn
        rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_app_ctor_lit E j c nlit lsc hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of a constructor applied to one literal. Relevance of the head is
   what erasure of that head reads. The value's relevance is `Good`'s premise.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_app_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_app_ctor_lit_val E lf c nlit lsc hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) => ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have he : erase E n 2 [] (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- A let whose body is a closed literal ζ-reduces to that literal.
   `instantiate` on a literal is the literal, so the bound value and the
   type do not appear in the normal form. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv nlit : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = some (.lit nlit) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, instantiate0, instantiate]
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`: `whnfFuel` of the let at fuel 1 is
   `whnfFuel` of the literal at fuel 0. -/
theorem norm_let_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv nlit : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .lit nlit := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (.lit nlit) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, instantiate0, instantiate]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_let_lit E j A kv nlit] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that let. Erasure reads relevance of the let, not of the
   literal value, so that hypothesis is extra. The witness is lowering
   fuel 2 and scm fuel 1. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv nlit : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_lit_val E lf A kv nlit hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 2 [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
          some (.letE (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
          emit 2 .i64 (.lit nlit) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat nlit) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A let that binds a literal and whose body is `bvar 0`. ζ substitutes
   that literal. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = some (.lit kv) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = .lit kv := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.lit kv) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_let_bvar_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kv := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_let_bvar E j A kv] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that let. Erasure of the body reads relevance of `bvar 0`
   under the let binding, so that hypothesis is extra. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_bvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n [.letBinding A (.lit kv)] (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_bvar_val E lf A kv hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kv) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 2 [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
          some (.letE (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
          emit 2 .i64 (.lit kv) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kv) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- β of a λ whose body is the bound index, applied to one literal.
   `instantiate` of `bvar 0` is the argument. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = some (.lit kv) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = .lit kv := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.lit kv) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_beta_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kv := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_lit E j A kv] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that application. Erasure of the λ reads relevance of the λ,
   and erasure of its body reads relevance of `bvar 0` under the assumption.
   The witness is lowering fuel 3: the λ body is erased one fuel under the
   application. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n [.assumption A] (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_lit_val E lf A kv hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kv) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
          some (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, hirrL, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
          Option.map]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kv) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kv) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A data type is an inductive constant applied to arguments, so it is not
   an arity. `irrelevant` of a term the checker types at such a `T` is then
   only whether the type of `T` is `Prop` as written. AdeqApp, AdeqLetE and
   AdeqConstDelta read this before erasure decides `□`. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem isArity_false_of_dataTy (E : ResolvedEnv) {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : DataTy E T) : isArity T = false := by
  obtain ⟨r, ls, args, m, hs, _, _⟩ := h
  cases T with
  | sort _ =>
      simp only [appsSpine] at hs
      exact Expr.noConfusion (congrArg Prod.fst hs)
  | pi _ _ =>
      simp only [appsSpine] at hs
      exact Expr.noConfusion (congrArg Prod.fst hs)
  | bvar _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | app _ _ => rfl
  | lam _ _ => rfl
  | letE _ _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl

theorem irrelevant_data (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T) :
    irrelevant E n [] e =
      match inferT E n [] T with
      | some U => isPropSort U
      | none => false := by
  have ha : isArity T = false := isArity_false_of_dataTy E hD
  simp only [irrelevant, hi, ha, Bool.false_or]

/- A non-literal the checker marks irrelevant erases to `□` at the next
   fuel. Sort and pi erase to `□` anyway. A literal ignores the test, so
   it is excluded. AdeqApp, AdeqLetE and AdeqConstDelta meet this before
   the relevant branch. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem erase_box_of_irrelevant (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx)
    (e : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n Γ e = true) (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ e = some .box := by
  cases e with
  | lit k => exact False.elim (hl k rfl)
  | sort _ => rfl
  | pi _ _ => rfl
  | bvar _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | const _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | app _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | lam _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | letE _ _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]

/- `□` runs to `box` and emits `refuse` at every positive fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_of_erase_box {S : SigTable} (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat)
    (he : erase E n (F + 1) [] e = some .box) :
    lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t e = refuse := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [he]
  cases t <;> rfl

/- Every lowering fuel of an irrelevant non-literal is `refuse`.
   Fuel 0 erases to nothing, which the pipeline also refuses. -/
theorem lowerF_irrelevant_refuses {S : SigTable} (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n [] e = true)
    (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) (F : Nat) :
    lowerF E n F (S := S) t e = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    exact lowerF_of_erase_box E n F t e (erase_box_of_irrelevant E n F [] e h hl)

/- Eval of that lowering is never `some w`. The conclusion of `Good` is
   false on this branch, so the three open lemmas hold here only when the
   other premises do not. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem eval_irrelevant_ne {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (w : Val)
    (h : irrelevant E n [] e = true) (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) (F lf : Nat) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) ≠ some w := by
  intro hE
  rw [lowerF_irrelevant_refuses E n t e h hl F] at hE
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w hE

/- `irrelevant_data` on the three answers of `inferT` for the data type.
   `false` is the relevant branch (`lowerF_const_delta_eval` and the
   app and let transports read it). `true` is the refuse branch
   (`eval_irrelevant_ne`). Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem irrelevant_data_ff (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T U : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = some U) (hp : isPropSort U = false) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = false := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]
  exact hp

theorem irrelevant_data_none (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = none) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = false := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]

theorem irrelevant_data_tt (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T U : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = some U) (hp : isPropSort U = true) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = true := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]
  exact hp

theorem const_ne_lit (r k : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    (.const r ls : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem app_ne_lit (f a : Expr Nat) (k : Nat) :
    (.app f a : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_lit (A v b : Expr Nat) (k : Nat) :
    (.letE A v b : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem list_get?_append_last {α : Type} : ∀ (xs : List α) (y : α),
    (xs ++ [y]).get? xs.length = some y
  | [], _ => rfl
  | _ :: xs, y => list_get?_append_last xs y

/- `run` on `apply`, as the joint match. Same equation as the passive
   simulation (`unfold run; rfl`). The AdeqApp β arm rewrites with it. -/
theorem run_apply_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (g a : DExpr) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.apply g a) =
      match run code F env g, run code F env a with
      | some (.clo l caps), some av =>
          match code.get? l with
          | some c => run code F (bindArg av caps) c.body
          | none => none
      | some (.ctor r args), some av => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
      | some (.rigid r args), some av => some (.rigid r (args ++ [av]))
      | some .box, some _ => some .box
      | _, _ => none := by
  unfold run
  rfl

/- `run` on `let`, as the value match. The AdeqLetE ζ arm rewrites with it. -/
theorem run_let_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (v b : DExpr) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.letE v b) =
      match run code F env v with
      | some vv => run code F (vv :: env) b
      | none => none := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_let_some (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (v b : DExpr)
    (vv : DVal) (h : run code F env v = some vv) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.letE v b) = run code F (vv :: env) b := by
  rw [run_let_eq, h]

/- A closure that captured nothing is that closure at every positive fuel.
   `mapM` of the empty capture list is `some []`. -/
theorem run_clo_nil (code : List Code) (F l : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.clo l []) = some (.clo l []) := by
  have h : run code (F + 1) env (.clo l []) =
      (([] : List Nat).mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (DVal.clo l) := by
    unfold run
    rfl
  rw [h, List.mapM_nil, Option.pure_def]
  rfl

/- Reynolds 1972 §8, empty capture: `apply (clo ℓ []) arg` runs the body in
   the one-element environment `[av]`. `convWith` appends that body after the
   inner code, so the label is `code.length`. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_clo_nil (code : List Code) (F l : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg body : DExpr) (av dv : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? l = some ⟨0, body⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av)
    (hb : run code (F + 1) [av] body = some dv) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo l []) arg) = some dv := by
  rw [run_apply_eq, run_clo_nil, ha]
  change (match code.get? l with
      | some c => run code (F + 1) (bindArg av []) c.body
      | none => none) = some dv
  rw [hc]
  exact hb

theorem run_apply_closed (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg body : DExpr) (av dv : DVal)
    (ha : run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 1) env arg = some av)
    (hb : run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 1) [av] body = some dv) :
    run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 2) env
      (.apply (.clo code.length []) arg) = some dv :=
  run_apply_clo_nil (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) F code.length env arg body av dv
    (list_get?_append_last code ⟨0, body⟩) ha hb

/- Slot 0 of a cons environment is the head, at every positive fuel.
   Reynolds 1972 §8 reads the argument from that slot. -/
theorem run_var0 (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (a : DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) (a :: env) (.var 0) = some a := by
  unfold run
  rfl

/- ζ of the bound index: the let returns the value it bound.
   `run_let_some` steps to slot 0. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem run_let_id (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (v : DExpr) (av : DVal) (h : run code (F + 1) env v = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.letE v (.var 0)) = some av := by
  rw [run_let_some code (F + 1) env v (.var 0) av h]
  exact run_var0 code F env av

/- β of a closure that captured nothing and whose body is slot 0.
   The label is 0. Reynolds 1972 §8, the identity. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_id (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg : DExpr) (av : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? 0 = some ⟨0, .var 0⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo 0 []) arg) = some av := by
  exact run_apply_clo_nil code F 0 env arg (.var 0) av av hc ha
    (run_var0 code F [] av)

/- β of a closure whose body is a literal. The argument is evaluated and
   then discarded: `run` on `.lit` does not read the environment.
   Reynolds 1972 §8. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_lit_body (code : List Code) (F l k : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg : DExpr) (av : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? l = some ⟨0, .lit k⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo l []) arg) = some (.lit k) := by
  have hb : run code (F + 1) [av] (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := by
    unfold run
    rfl
  exact run_apply_clo_nil code F l env arg (.lit k) av (.lit k) hc ha hb

/- A let whose body is the bound index defunctionalizes as that let.
   The body's renaming sends slot 0 to slot 0, and it allocates no code.
   Danvy–Nielsen PPDP 2001. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem defunc_let_bvar0 (lv : LExpr) :
    defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0)) =
      (DExpr.letE (defunc lv).1 (.var 0), (defunc lv).2) := rfl

/- An application of the identity λ defunctionalizes as apply of a
   closure at label 0 with an empty capture. The argument is converted
   against the one code entry that closure points at. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_app_lam_bvar0 (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la) =
      (let q := convWith capRen id [{ ncap := 0, body := .var 0 }] la
       (DExpr.apply (DExpr.clo 0 []) q.1, q.2)) := rfl

/- ζ of `bvar 0` is the bound term, one whnf fuel earlier.
   `instantiate0` of that index is the term. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_let_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = whnfFuel E k v := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 v (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 v (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = v := rfl
  rw [hzeta, hsub]

/- β of the identity λ is the argument, one whnf fuel earlier.
   `[] ++ [arg]` is the cons the lam arm matches. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = whnfFuel E k arg := by
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 arg (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = arg := rfl
  rw [hbeta, hsub]

/- One β step, for an arbitrary body. `foldApps` of the empty tail is the
   instantiation. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A body arg : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A body) arg) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 arg body) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]

/- One ζ step, for an arbitrary body. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_zeta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v body : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v body) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 v body) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]

/- Heads `whnfFuel` does not step. Fuel 0 is `none`. -/
theorem whnf_zero_none {E : ResolvedEnv} {e v : Expr Nat}
    (h : whnfFuel E 0 e = some v) : False := by
  simp only [whnfFuel] at h
  cases h

theorem whnf_sort_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (l : Level) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.sort l) = some (.sort l) := rfl

theorem whnf_lam_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lam A b) = some (.lam A b) := rfl

theorem whnf_pi_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.pi A B) = some (.pi A B) := rfl

theorem whnf_bvar_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k i : Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := rfl

theorem whnf_lit_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k t : Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit t) = some (.lit t) := rfl

/- A rigid constant is its own weak head, at every positive fuel. -/
theorem whnf_rigid_const {E : ResolvedEnv} (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hn : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hn]

/- A successful norm of the bound term is a norm of the identity let,
   one fuel later. Same shift as `norm_const_delta_of_body`. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) v = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k v with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_let_id E k A v]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) v = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k v w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = norm E (k + 2) v := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) v val hn

/- A successful norm of the argument is a norm of the identity β,
   one fuel later. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) arg = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k arg with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_beta_id E k A arg]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) arg = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k arg w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = norm E (k + 2) arg := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) arg val hn

/- Eval of a relevant let at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the emitted value of
   the two erasures' defunctionalized let, run at fuel `F`.
   `erase_let_keep` is the erasure step. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem lowerF_let_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (A v b : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A v b) = false)
    (lv lb : LExpr)
    (hv : erase E n F [] v = some lv)
    (hb : erase E n F (.letBinding A v :: []) b = some lb)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc (.letE lv lb)).2 F [] (defunc (.letE lv lb)).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.letE A v b)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  have hee : erase E n (F + 1) [] (.letE A v b) = some (.letE lv lb) := by
    simp only [erase_let_keep E n F [] A v b hirr, hv, hb]
  simp only [hee]
  have hr' := run_mono (defunc (.letE lv lb)).2 F (F + 1) []
      (defunc (.letE lv lb)).1 dv (Nat.le_succ F) hr
  simp only [hr']
  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t dv w
    (Nat.le_succ F) he

/- Eval of a relevant application at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the emitted
   value of the two erasures' defunctionalized application, run at fuel `F`.
   `erase_app_keep` is the erasure step. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lowerF_app_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (g a : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app g a) = false)
    (lg la : LExpr)
    (hg : erase E n F [] g = some lg)
    (ha : erase E n F [] a = some la)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc (.app lg la)).2 F [] (defunc (.app lg la)).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.app g a)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  have hee : erase E n (F + 1) [] (.app g a) = some (.app lg la) := by
    simp only [erase_app_keep E n F [] g a hirr, hg, ha]
  simp only [hee]
  have hr' := run_mono (defunc (.app lg la)).2 F (F + 1) []
      (defunc (.app lg la)).1 dv (Nat.le_succ F) hr
  simp only [hr']
  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t dv w
    (Nat.le_succ F) he

/- A successful norm of the identity let is a norm of the bound term
   at the same fuel. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_id_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) v = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k v = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_let_id E k A v]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) v = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k v w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = norm E (k + 2) v := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- A successful norm of the identity application is a norm of the
   argument at the same fuel. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_id_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) arg = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k arg = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_beta_id E k A arg]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) arg = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k arg w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) =
        norm E (k + 2) arg := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- `foldApps` rebuilds the spine `appsSpine` peeled. The head's own
   arguments stay in front of the new ones. -/
theorem appsSpine_foldApps (f : Expr Nat) :
    ∀ xs, appsSpine (foldApps f xs) = ((appsSpine f).1, (appsSpine f).2 ++ xs)
  | [] => by
      simp only [foldApps, List.append_nil]
  | x :: xs => by
      rw [foldApps, appsSpine_foldApps (.app f x) xs]
      have happ : appsSpine (.app f x) =
          ((appsSpine f).1, (appsSpine f).2 ++ [x]) := by
        simp only [appsSpine]
      rw [happ]
      have ha : ((appsSpine f).2 ++ [x]) ++ xs =
          (appsSpine f).2 ++ (x :: xs) := by
        rw [List.append_assoc]
        rfl
      exact congrArg (fun ys => ((appsSpine f).1, ys)) ha

/- One β step on a spine whose head is a λ. The first argument is
   substituted; the rest of the spine stays. `whnf_beta` is the
   one-argument case (`args = []`). Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
      (.lam A b, a :: args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]

/- A successful norm of the β-reduct is a norm of the λ-spine, one fuel
   later. The two `norm`s share the head `whnf_beta_spine` produces, and
   `norm_mono` lifts the reduct. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_beta_spine E k A b a args]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards: a successful norm of the λ-spine is a
   norm of the β-reduct. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_beta_spine E k A b a args]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- One ζ step on a spine whose head is a let. `whnf_zeta` is the empty
   spine. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_zeta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v b) args) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.letE A v b) args) = (.letE A v b, args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]

/- A successful norm of the ζ-reduct is a norm of the let-spine, one fuel
   later. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_zeta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v0 b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_zeta_spine E k A v0 b args]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_zeta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v0 b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_zeta_spine E k A v0 b args]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- One δ step on a spine whose head is a transparent constant.
   `whnf_const_delta` is the empty spine. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem whnf_delta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat))
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some body) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = (.const r ls, args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]
  simp only [hb]

/- A successful norm of the δ-reduct is a norm of the constant spine, one
   fuel later. `norm_const_delta_of_body` is the empty spine. Not
   AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_delta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_delta_spine E k r ls body args ht]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps body args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_delta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_delta_spine E k r ls body args ht]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps body args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- One δ, for an arbitrary body, once that body evaluates to the same
   scm value. `norm_delta_spine_eq` at the empty spine reads the body's
   normal form off the constant, and `lowerF_const_delta_eval` moves the
   evaluation across erasure. Relevance of the constant is a hypothesis:
   `Good` does not supply it. The body hypothesis is the eval, not
   `Good` of the body. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem good_const_delta_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hbody : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf b = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t b) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf _
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          have hn' : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) []) = some v := hn
          have hbn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps b []) = some v :=
            norm_delta_spine_eq E k r ls b [] v hb hn'
          have hbb : norm E (k + 2) b = some v := hbn
          obtain ⟨F, lfe, he⟩ :=
            hbody (k + 2) fv v t w hbb hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf
          exact ⟨F + 1, lfe,
            lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n F r lfe ls b t w hirr hb he⟩

/- Eval of an identity let at fuel `F + 3` is eval of the emitted value
   of the bound term's erasure, run at fuel `F + 1`. The body erases to
   slot 0. `erase_mono` lifts that erasure one fuel, and `run_let_id`
   returns the bound value. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem lowerF_let_id_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (A v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.letBinding A v :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (lv : LExpr)
    (hv : erase E n (F + 1) [] v = some lv)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc lv).2 (F + 1) [] (defunc lv).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 3) (S := S) t (.letE A v (.bvar 0))) = some w := by
  have hv2 : erase E n (F + 2) [] v = some lv :=
    erase_mono E n (F + 1) (F + 2) [] v lv (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) hv
  have hb : erase E n (F + 2) (.letBinding A v :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
  have he2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 2) t dv) = some w :=
    emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] (F + 1) (F + 2) t dv w
      (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) he
  have hrlet : run (defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0))).2 (F + 2) []
      (defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0))).1 = some dv := by
    rw [defunc_let_bvar0]
    exact run_let_id (defunc lv).2 F [] (defunc lv).1 dv hr
  exact lowerF_let_eval progs E n (F + 2) lf A v (.bvar 0) t w hirr lv (.bvar 0)
    hv2 hb dv hrlet he2

/- Level equality is an equivalence. `eval` here is the level interpreter,
   not bootstrap `eval`. -/
theorem eqN_refl (l : Level) : eqN l l := fun _ => rfl

theorem eqN_symm {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN l₁ l₂) : eqN l₂ l₁ :=
  fun ρ => (h ρ).symm

theorem eqN_trans {l₁ l₂ l₃ : Level} (h₁ : eqN l₁ l₂) (h₂ : eqN l₂ l₃) : eqN l₁ l₃ :=
  fun ρ => (h₁ ρ).trans (h₂ ρ)

theorem eqN_succ {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN l₁ l₂) : eqN (.succ l₁) (.succ l₂) := by
  intro ρ
  simp only [Rsx.eval, h ρ]

/- `Sort (succ l)` is not extensionally `Sort 0`. -/
theorem eqN_succ_ne_zero (l : Level) (h : eqN (.succ l) .zero) : False := by
  have hρ : Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) (.succ l) =
      Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) .zero := h (fun _ => some 0)
  simp only [Rsx.eval] at hρ
  cases hv : Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) l with
  | none =>
      rw [hv] at hρ
      simp only [Option.map] at hρ
      cases hρ
  | some n =>
      rw [hv] at hρ
      simp only [Option.map] at hρ
      injection hρ with hn
      exact Nat.succ_ne_zero n hn

/- `foldApps f (xs ++ [y])` is an application, never a sort. -/
theorem foldApps_append_ne_sort (f : Expr Nat) (xs : List (Expr Nat)) (y : Expr Nat)
    (l : Level) : foldApps f (xs ++ [y]) ≠ .sort l := by
  induction xs generalizing f with
  | nil =>
      simp only [List.nil_append, foldApps]
      intro h
      cases h
  | cons x xs ih =>
      simp only [List.cons_append, foldApps]
      exact ih (.app f x)

/- A derived iota left-hand side is `recCall`, a nonempty application spine. -/
theorem iotaLhs_ne_sort {E : ResolvedEnv} (w : IotaWitness E) (l : Level) :
    iotaLhsOf w ≠ .sort l := by
  unfold iotaLhsOf recCall
  exact foldApps_append_ne_sort (.const w.recRef w.ls) w.preMajor (ctorMajor w) l

/- The same spine is never a constant. -/
theorem foldApps_append_ne_const (f : Expr Nat) (xs : List (Expr Nat)) (y : Expr Nat)
    (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) : foldApps f (xs ++ [y]) ≠ .const r ls := by
  induction xs generalizing f with
  | nil =>
      simp only [List.nil_append, foldApps]
      intro h
      cases h
  | cons x xs ih =>
      simp only [List.cons_append, foldApps]
      exact ih (.app f x)

theorem iotaLhs_ne_const {E : ResolvedEnv} (w : IotaWitness E) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    iotaLhsOf w ≠ .const r ls := by
  unfold iotaLhsOf recCall
  exact foldApps_append_ne_const (.const w.recRef w.ls) w.preMajor (ctorMajor w) r ls

/- A derived iota is an application spine, so it is not a constant. -/
theorem derivedIota_ne_const {E : ResolvedEnv} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {rhs : Expr Nat}
    (h : DerivedIota E (.const r ls) rhs) : False :=
  (DerivedIota.rec (motive := fun lhs _ _ => lhs = .const r ls → False)
    (fun w => iotaLhs_ne_const w r ls) h) rfl

/- A sort is typed at `Sort (succ l)` up to `TyConvT`. The chain is the
   `HasTyT.conv` spine; no `ConvT` inversion. Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp,
   or AdeqLetE. -/
/- Same fact when the subject is already a sort. The constructor level is
   the index, so the sort arm is a term. -/
def hasTyT_sort_principal_at {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {l : Level} {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ (.sort l) T) :
    Σ' (l' : Level) (_ : eqN l' (.succ l)), TyConvT E n Γ (.sort l') T :=
  match h with
  | .sort _ _ => ⟨.succ l, ⟨eqN_refl _, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩
  | .conv Γ _ A B u hsub hc =>
      match hasTyT_sort_principal_at hsub with
      | ⟨l', ⟨heq, ht⟩⟩ =>
          ⟨l', ⟨heq, TyConvT.trans Γ (.sort l') A B ht (TyConvT.of Γ A B u hc)⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

def hasTyT_sort_principal {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ e T) (he : e = .sort l) :
    Σ' (l' : Level) (_ : eqN l' (.succ l)), TyConvT E n Γ (.sort l') T := by
  subst he
  exact hasTyT_sort_principal_at h

/- A constant is typed at its instantiated declared type up to `TyConvT`.
   Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def hasTyT_const_principal_at {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ (.const r ls) T) :
    Σ' (m : CheckedMember) (_ : E.members r = some m)
        (_ : ls.length = m.arity) (_ : levelsBounded n ls = true),
      TyConvT E n Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) T :=
  match h with
  | .const _ _ _ m hres hlen hwf =>
      ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩⟩⟩
  | .conv Γ _ A B u hsub hc =>
      match hasTyT_const_principal_at hsub with
      | ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf, ht⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
          ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf,
            TyConvT.trans Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) A B ht
              (TyConvT.of Γ A B u hc)⟩⟩⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

def hasTyT_const_principal {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ e T) (he : e = .const r ls) :
    Σ' (m : CheckedMember) (_ : E.members r = some m)
        (_ : ls.length = m.arity) (_ : levelsBounded n ls = true),
      TyConvT E n Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) T := by
  subst he
  exact hasTyT_const_principal_at h

/- A transparent constant whose body is a non-constructor head has no scm
   value. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_rigid {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hnot : ∀ m, E.members c = some m → ¬ m.mclass = .constructorM) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  have hv := norm_const_ctor_val E lf r c ls lsc hb hnone hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_const_not_ctor E fv c lsc hnot] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-- a lowering keeps every value evalLF gets from it when its fuel grows. -/
def FuelStable {S : SigTable} (low : Lowering S) (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F F' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (lf : Nat) (w : Val),
    F ≤ F' →
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (low E n F t e) = some w →
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (low E n F' t e) = some w

theorem lowerF_fuelStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    FuelStable (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs :=
  fun E n F F' t e lf w hF h => lowerF_evalStable progs E n F F' t e lf w hF h

/-- mutant: the output reads the lowering fuel (its parity). -/
def fuelParity {S : SigTable} : Lowering S := fun _ _ F t _ =>
  match t with
  | .i64 => .litI ((F % 2 : Nat) : Int)
  | _ => refuse

theorem fuelParity_not_fuelStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ FuelStable (fuelParity (S := S)) progs := by
  intro h
  have h0 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (fuelParity (S := S) adqEnv 0 0 .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 0) :=
    eval_litI progs 0 (by decide)
  have h1 := h adqEnv 0 0 1 .i64 (.lit 0) 1 (.int 0) (by decide) h0
  have h2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (fuelParity (S := S) adqEnv 0 1 .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 1) :=
    eval_litI progs 1 (by decide)
  rw [h2] at h1
  exact absurd (Val.int.inj (Option.some.inj h1)) (by decide)

/-! ## Controls (`#guard`): a closed environment and small closed data-typed terms

Members (05 §3 order for Nat, as `natExpand` requires: 0 `N`, 1 `zero`, 2 `succ`):
0 N, 1 zero, 2 succ, 4 True : Prop, 5 True.intro, 6 Bool, 7 false, 8 true,
9 P, 10 P.mk : N → N → P, 11 two := succ (succ zero), 12 addTwo := λ x. succ (succ x),
13 ax : N (axiom), 14 thm : True (theorem). -/

def cN : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def cZero : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def cSucc : Expr Nat := .const 2 []
def cTrue : Expr Nat := .const 4 []
def cIntro : Expr Nat := .const 5 []
def cMk : Expr Nat := .const 10 []

def ctlEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩
    | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩
    | 4 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
    | 5 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩
    | 6 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 7 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
    | 8 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
    | 9 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 10 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩
    | 11 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩
    | 12 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
              some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩
    | 13 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩
    | 14 => some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩
    | _ => none

/-- scm sum type with `k` summands, each `list τ`. -/
def sumL (k : Nat) (τ : BootTy) : BootTy := .sum (List.replicate k (.list τ))

def tyNat1 : BootTy := sumL 3 .i64
def tyNat2 : BootTy := sumL 3 tyNat1
def tyNat3 : BootTy := sumL 3 tyNat2

def optValEq : Option Val → Option Val → Bool
  | some a, some b => valEq a b
  | none, none => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- the value side: `scmValOf (norm t)`. -/
def obs (E : ResolvedEnv) (e : Expr Nat) : Option Val :=
  match norm E 64 e with
  | some v => scmValOf E 64 v
  | none => none

/-- the scm side: `evalLF` of a lowered term (empty program table). -/
def runLowered {t : BootTy} (b : BootExpr [] [] t) : Option Val :=
  Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA .nil 64 [] b

/-- positive control: the value side is data, and evalLF of the lowering equals it. -/
def agrees (low : (t : BootTy) → Expr Nat → BootExpr [] [] t) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : Bool :=
  (obs E e).isSome && optValEq (runLowered (low t e)) (obs E e)

def ref (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t := Rsx.lower ctlEnv (t := t) e

-- the terms
def g01 : Expr Nat := .lit 5
def g02 : Expr Nat := cZero
def g03 : Expr Nat := .app cSucc (.lit 4)
def g04 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))) (.lit 4)              -- β
def g05 : Expr Nat := .letE cN (.lit 7) (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))                     -- ζ
def g06 : Expr Nat := .const 11 []                                                 -- δ
def g07 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cTrue (.lit 3)) cIntro                            -- proof arg erased
def g08 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- type arg erased
  .app (.app (.lam (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.lam (.bvar 0) (.bvar 0))) cN) (.lit 9)
def g09 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- higher order
  .app (.lam (.pi cN cN) (.app (.bvar 0) (.lit 1))) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))
def g10 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- capture
  .app (.app (.lam cN (.lam cN (.app (.app cMk (.bvar 0)) (.bvar 1)))) (.lit 1)) (.lit 2)
def g11 : Expr Nat := .const 8 []
def g12 : Expr Nat := .app (.const 12 []) (.lit 0)                                 -- δ to a λ
def g13 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- let-bound λ
  .letE (.pi cN cN) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))
    (.app (.bvar 0) (.app (.bvar 0) (.lit 0)))
def g14 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cTrue (.app cSucc cZero)) (.const 14 [])           -- theorem arg erased

-- 14 positive controls: evalLF (Rsx.lower t) = scmValOf (norm t), and is data
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g01
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g02
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g03
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g04
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g05
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat3 g06
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g07
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g08
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g09
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv (sumL 9 .i64) g11
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g12
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g13
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g14

-- the controls exercise the stages they name: erasure removed the arguments of g07, g08, g14
#guard erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g07 = some (.app (.lam (.lit 3)) .box)
#guard erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g08 = some (.app (.app (.lam (.lam (.bvar 0))) .box) (.lit 9))
-- defunctionalization of g10: two λ records, the inner one capturing one variable
#guard (defunc ((erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g10).getD .box)).2.map Code.ncap = [1, 0]

-- refusals agree with the value side: no data value, and the lowering evaluates to none
def g15 : Expr Nat := .lam cN (.bvar 0)          -- a function: not data
def g16 : Expr Nat := .const 13 []               -- an axiom: rigid, not data
#guard (obs ctlEnv g15).isNone && (runLowered (ref tyNat1 g15)).isNone
#guard (obs ctlEnv g16).isNone && (runLowered (ref tyNat1 g16)).isNone

-- gap witnesses (reports/rsxlower/GAPS.md): the value side has data that no BootExpr of
-- the requested type produces
def g17 : Expr Nat := .app (.app cMk (.const 11 [])) (.lit 3)   -- fields: constructor and literal
def g18 : Expr Nat := .lit 9223372036854775808                  -- 2^63, beyond i64
#guard (obs ctlEnv g17).isSome && (runLowered (ref (sumL 11 .i64) g17)).isNone
#guard (obs ctlEnv g18).isSome && (runLowered (ref .i64 g18)).isNone

/-! ### Negative controls: planted lowering mutants are refused by the same check -/

/-- erasure mutant: treats every term whose type's type is any sort as irrelevant
    (erases data). -/
def irrelevantAnySort (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) : Bool :=
  match inferT E n Γ e with
  | some T =>
      isArity T ||
        (match inferT E n Γ T with
         | some (.sort _) => true
         | _ => false)
  | none => false

/-- defunctionalization mutant: captured slot `k` read at `k` instead of `1 + k`. -/
def capRenOff (fs : List Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => (idxOf i fs).getD fs.length

/-- fuel-stage mutant: `apply` binds the argument after the captured values. -/
def bindLast (a : DVal) (caps : List DVal) : List DVal := caps ++ [a]

/-- emission mutant: constructor fields in reverse order. -/
def fieldsRev (args : List DVal) : List DVal := (relevantArgs args).reverse

def mutErase (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (eraseWith (irrelevantAnySort ctlEnv 0) noGlobals ctlEnv) defunc run emit defaultFuel t e
def mutDefunc (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) (convWith capRenOff id []) run emit defaultFuel t e
def mutRun (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc (runWith bindLast) emit defaultFuel t e
def mutEmit (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc run (emitWith fieldsRev) defaultFuel t e

-- the reference is the pipeline with the reference stages
example : ref = pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc run emit defaultFuel := rfl

#guard !(agrees mutErase ctlEnv tyNat1 g03)
#guard !(agrees mutDefunc ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)
#guard !(agrees mutRun ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)
#guard !(agrees mutEmit ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)

/-! ### Counterexample to the step-4 statement: a Prop-typed data value

`True.intro : True` in `ctlEnv` (member 5; `True` = member 4, an inductive in `Prop`).
`DataTy` holds (`True` is an inductive), `norm` returns `True.intro`, `scmValOf` gives
`.inj 5 (.list [])`, `relevantSpine` holds (no fields), and the value fits
`sumL 6 .i64`. Erasure maps the term to `□` (its type's type is `Prop`: Letouzey's test,
Lean's compiler erases it too), so the lowering refuses at every fuel. Hence the
reference family does NOT meet `adequacyStatementNoRoot` (the step-4 form), and the
statement on main adds `irrelevant E n [] v = false`, which this witness violates
(`cIntro_irrelevant`). -/

def cIntroTyNat : BootTy := sumL 6 .i64

def cIntroTy : HasTyT ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  .const [] 5 [] ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩ rfl rfl rfl

theorem cIntroData : DataTy ctlEnv (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  ⟨4, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cIntroNorm : norm ctlEnv 2 cIntro = some cIntro := rfl
theorem cIntroVal : scmValOf ctlEnv 1 cIntro = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem cIntroRel : relevantSpine ctlEnv 0 1 cIntro = true := rfl
theorem cIntroFits : valFits 1 cIntroTyNat (.inj 5 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem cIntro_irrelevant : irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro = true := by decide

/-- the reference lowering of `True.intro` is the refusing term at every fuel and type. -/
theorem lowerF_cIntro {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF ctlEnv 0 F (S := S) t cIntro = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] (.const 5 []) = true := cIntro_irrelevant
    have he : erase ctlEnv 0 (F + 1) [] cIntro = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, cIntro, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- the counterexample: the reference family does not meet the step-4 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_noRoot {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementNoRoot (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h ctlEnv 0 2 1 cIntro _ cIntro cIntroTyNat (.inj 5 (.list []))
    cIntroTy cIntroData cIntroNorm cIntroVal cIntroRel cIntroFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF ctlEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) cIntroTyNat cIntro) = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_cIntro] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- the same witness as a gap guard: data on the value side, refused by the lowering, and
-- excluded from the statement on main by its root-relevance premise
#guard (obs ctlEnv cIntro).isSome && (runLowered (ref cIntroTyNat cIntro)).isNone &&
  irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro

/-! ### Counterexample to the session-7 statement: a transparent body not of its type

`badEnv` is `ctlEnv` plus member 15, a transparent definition `c : True` whose body is
`zero : N`. `HasTyT.const` types `c` at its declared type `True` (no rule reads the body;
only `ConvT.delta` does, and it demands the body typed), so `DataTy` holds. `norm` unfolds
`c` (`whnfFuel` δ never reads a type) to `zero`, whose value `.inj 1 (.list [])` is relevant
(`zero : N`, `N : Type`) and fits `tyNat1`. Erasure tests `c` before δ: its type's type is
`Prop`, so it erases to `□` and the lowering refuses at every fuel. Hence the reference
family does NOT meet `adequacyStatementUntypedEnv` (the session-7 form), and the statement
on main adds `BodiesTyped E n` (MetaCoq's `wf Σ`, the premise of `ConvT.delta`). The body
is outside `BodiesTyped`: the certified checker `inferT` types it at `N`, not `True`
(guard below); a proof that no `HasTyT` derivation types it at `True` needs a model of
`ConvT` and is not given. -/

def badEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 15 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩
    | r => ctlEnv.members r

def cBad : Expr Nat := .const 15 []

def cBadTy : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cBad (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  .const [] 15 [] ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩ rfl rfl rfl

/- Member 1 of badEnv is zero, declared at N. -/
theorem badEnv_zero : badEnv.members 1 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl

/- HasTyT of zero at True is a TyConvT from N to True.
   Not the negation, and not AdeqConstDelta. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_of_cZero
    (h : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cZero cTrue) :
    TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue := by
  match hasTyT_const_principal h rfl with
  | ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨_, ⟨_, ht⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
      have hm : m = ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_zero] at hres
        injection hres with hm
        exact hm.symm
      subst hm
      exact ht

/- One TyConvT step. The ends are equal, or a ConvT at a sort reaches a
   middle that still type-converts to the right end. No ConvT inversion.
   Not the negation of TyConvT from cN to cTrue, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def tyConvT_step {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {A B : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT E n Γ A B) :
    PSum (A = B)
      (Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT E n Γ A C (.sort u)),
        TyConvT E n Γ C B) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => PSum.inl rfl
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      PSum.inr ⟨B, ⟨u, ⟨hc, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩⟩
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyConvT_step h1 with
      | PSum.inl heq =>
          Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X =>
              PSum (X = B)
                (Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT E n Γ X C (.sort u)),
                  TyConvT E n Γ C B))
            (tyConvT_step h2) (Eq.symm heq)
      | PSum.inr ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, ht⟩⟩⟩ =>
          PSum.inr ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, TyConvT.trans Γ C mid B ht h2⟩⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

/- TyConvT reads the same backwards. The one-step arm is ConvT.symm.
   No ConvT inversion. -/
def tyConvT_symm {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {A B : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT E n Γ A B) : TyConvT E n Γ B A :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => TyConvT.refl _ _
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      TyConvT.of Γ B A u (ConvT.symm Γ A B (.sort u) hc)
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      TyConvT.trans Γ B mid A (tyConvT_symm h2) (tyConvT_symm h1)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- Two type conversions into one end compose. -/
def tyConvT_of_to_same {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx}
    {A B C : Expr Nat}
    (hA : TyConvT E n Γ A C) (hB : TyConvT E n Γ B C) :
    TyConvT E n Γ A B :=
  TyConvT.trans Γ A C B hA (tyConvT_symm hB)

/- N and True are different constants. -/
theorem cN_ne_cTrue : cN ≠ cTrue := by
  intro h
  unfold cN cTrue at h
  injection h with hr hls
  cases hr

/- TyConvT from N to True is a ConvT from N at a sort, followed by a
   TyConvT to True. The equality arm is empty. Not the negation. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_step
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) :
    Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN C (.sort u)),
      TyConvT badEnv 0 [] C cTrue :=
  match tyConvT_step h with
  | PSum.inl heq => absurd heq cN_ne_cTrue
  | PSum.inr s => s

/- Member 0 of badEnv is N, an inductive, not a transparent definition. -/
theorem badEnv_N :
    badEnv.members 0 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl

theorem badEnv_not_transparent_zero (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members 0 = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true) : False := by
  have hm : m = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := by
    rw [badEnv_N] at hres
    injection hres with hm
    exact hm.symm
  subst hm
  cases htr

/- One ConvT step whose left end is N. Beta, zeta, eta, congruence,
   literal, sort, and delta are not in the view: N is not those
   left-hand sides, and member 0 is not transparent. Iota is an
   application spine. The symm, trans, proof-irrelevance, and tyConv
   arms are exposed, not discharged. Not the negation of TyConvT from
   N to True, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvCN : Expr Nat → Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl (T : Expr Nat) : ConvCN cN T
  | symm (b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] b cN T) : ConvCN b T
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvCN b T
  | consts (ls' : List Level) (T : Expr Nat) (h : eqNList [] ls') :
      ConvCN (.const 0 ls') T
  | irr (b T P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvCN b T
  | ty (b A T : Expr Nat) (u : Level)
      (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b A)
      (hA : ConvT badEnv 0 [] A T (.sort u)) : ConvCN b T

def convT_cN_view {b T : Expr Nat} (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b T) : ConvCN b T :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvCN.refl T
  | .symm _ x _ _ hinner => ConvCN.symm x T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvCN.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .delta _ _ _ m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const hdi)
  | .consts _ _ _ ls' m _ _ _ _ heq =>
      ConvCN.consts ls' (instantiateLevels [] m.mtype) heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvCN.irr b P P hP hp hq
  | .tyConv _ _ _ A _ u hsub hA => ConvCN.ty b A T u hsub hA

/- TyConvT from N to True starts with one of those ConvT shapes. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_view (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) :
    Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvCN C (.sort u)),
      TyConvT badEnv 0 [] C cTrue :=
  match tyConvT_cN_cTrue_step h with
  | ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, ht⟩⟩⟩ => ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨convT_cN_view hc, ht⟩⟩⟩

/- `eqNList [] ls` is the nil clause, so the level list is empty. -/
theorem eqNList_nil_left {ls : List Level} (h : eqNList [] ls) : ls = [] :=
  match ls, h with
  | [], _ => rfl
  | _ :: _, h => nomatch h

theorem const0_nil_eq {ls : List Level} (h : eqNList [] ls) :
    (.const 0 ls : Expr Nat) = cN := by
  cases eqNList_nil_left h
  rfl

theorem const0_ne_cTrue (ls : List Level) : (.const 0 ls : Expr Nat) ≠ cTrue := by
  intro h
  unfold cTrue at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

theorem const4_ne_cN (ls : List Level) : (.const 4 ls : Expr Nat) ≠ cN := by
  intro h
  unfold cN at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

/- Member 4 of badEnv is True, an inductive, not a transparent definition. -/
theorem badEnv_True :
    badEnv.members 4 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := rfl

theorem badEnv_not_transparent_four (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members 4 = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true) : False := by
  have hm : m = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := by
    rw [badEnv_True] at hres
    injection hres with hm
    exact hm.symm
  subst hm
  cases htr

/- One ConvT step from N, with type change stripped. The right end is
   the index. Symmetry, transitivity, and proof irrelevance stay.
   Recursing through tyConv forgets the type annotation. Not the
   negation of TyConvT from N to True. -/
inductive ConvCNty : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvCNty cN
  | symm (b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] b cN T) : ConvCNty b
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvCNty b
  | consts (ls' : List Level) (h : eqNList [] ls') : ConvCNty (.const 0 ls')
  | irr (b P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvCNty b

def convT_cN_core {b T : Expr Nat} (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b T) : ConvCNty b :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvCNty.refl
  | .symm _ x _ _ hinner => ConvCNty.symm x T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvCNty.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .delta _ _ _ m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const hdi)
  | .consts _ _ _ ls' _ _ _ _ _ heq => ConvCNty.consts ls' heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvCNty.irr b P hP hp hq
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convT_cN_core hsub
termination_by sizeOf h

/- Both constants typed at one `P` send their declared types to `P`,
   so `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are type-convertible. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common (P : Expr Nat)
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
    (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cTrue P) :
    TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero) := by
  match hasTyT_const_principal hp rfl with
  | ⟨mN, ⟨hresN, ⟨_, ⟨_, htN⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
    match hasTyT_const_principal hq rfl with
    | ⟨mT, ⟨hresT, ⟨_, ⟨_, htT⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
      have hmN : mN = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_N] at hresN
        injection hresN with hm
        exact hm.symm
      have hmT : mT = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_True] at hresT
        injection hresT with hm
        exact hm.symm
      subst hmN
      subst hmT
      exact tyConvT_of_to_same htN htT

/- What remains of a conversion between N and True after a reflexive
   left half and type change are consumed. `trans` keeps a left half
   that is not reflexivity. `transR` keeps the swapped derivation.
   `sortGap` is the `Sort 1` / `Sort 0` type conversion that proof
   irrelevance produces. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvNT : Type where
  | trans (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m cTrue T) : ConvNT
  | transR (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cTrue m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m cN T) : ConvNT
  | sortGap (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero)) : ConvNT

/- Delta toward N from a constant equal to True. The only body
   `instantiateLevels` sends to `cN` is `const 0 []`, so the head is
   member 4, which is not transparent. -/
theorem convStuckR_delta_false (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact badEnv_not_transparent_four m hres htr

theorem instLevels_bvar_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (i : Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.bvar i) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_sort_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.sort l) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_app_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (f x : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.app f x) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_lam_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.lam a b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_pi_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.pi a b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_letE_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a v b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.letE a v b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_lit_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (t : Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.lit t) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_const_succ_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (n : Nat) (ms : List Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.const (n + 1) ms) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

theorem instLevels_const_zero_cons_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (l : Level) (ms : List Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.const 0 (l :: ms)) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  injection h with hr hms
  cases hms

theorem app_ne_cN (f x : Expr Nat) (h : .app f x = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem app_ne_cTrue (f x : Expr Nat) (h : .app f x = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_cN (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : .letE A v b = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_cTrue (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : .letE A v b = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem bvar_ne_cN (i : Nat) (h : (.bvar i : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem bvar_ne_cTrue (i : Nat) (h : (.bvar i : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem lit_ne_cN (t : Nat) (h : (.lit t : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem lit_ne_cTrue (t : Nat) (h : (.lit t : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem lam_ne_cN (A b : Expr Nat) (h : .lam A b = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem lam_ne_cTrue (A b : Expr Nat) (h : .lam A b = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem pi_ne_cN (A B : Expr Nat) (h : .pi A B = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem pi_ne_cTrue (A B : Expr Nat) (h : .pi A B = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem sort_ne_cN (l : Level) (h : (.sort l : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem sort_ne_cTrue (l : Level) (h : (.sort l : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem convStuck_delta_false (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr

theorem consts_cN_ne_cTrue (r : Nat) (ls ls' : List Level)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cN) (hb : (.const r ls' : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cN at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact const0_ne_cTrue ls' hb

theorem consts_cTrue_ne_cN (r : Nat) (ls ls' : List Level)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cTrue) (hb : (.const r ls' : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact const4_ne_cN ls' hb

/- Both ends stay variables, so `instantiateLevels` unifies. The
   equalities say which end is N and which is True. Symmetry swaps
   those equalities and recurses on the raw subderivation. Not
   `¬ TyConvT`. -/
mutual
def convStuck {a b T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = cN) (hb : b = cTrue) : ConvNT :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner => convStuckAtTrue hinner hb ha
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      ConvNT.trans m T
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X m T) h1 ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] m X T) h2 hb)
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convStuck hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cN (.lam A body) arg ha)
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cN A value body ha)
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (bvar_ne_cN i ha)
  | .delta _ r ls m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (convStuck_delta_false r ls m hres htr ha)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ =>
      False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => DerivedIota badEnv X b) hdi ha))
  | .lit _ t _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lit_ne_cN t ha)
  | .app _ f _ x _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cN f x ha)
  | .lam _ A _ body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lam_ne_cN A body ha)
  | .pi _ A _ B _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (pi_ne_cN A B ha)
  | .letE _ A _ v _ body _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cN A v body ha)
  | .sorts _ l _ _ => False.elim (sort_ne_cN l ha)
  | .consts _ r ls ls' _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (consts_cN_ne_cTrue r ls ls' ha hb)
  | .eta _ f A _ _ =>
      False.elim (lam_ne_cN A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)) ha)
  | .irr _ P _ _ _ hp hq =>
      ConvNT.sortGap (tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common P
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hp ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hq hb))
termination_by sizeOf h

def convStuckAtTrue {a b T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = cTrue) (hb : b = cN) : ConvNT :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm hb) ha))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner => convStuck hinner hb ha
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      ConvNT.transR m T
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X m T) h1 ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] m X T) h2 hb)
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convStuckAtTrue hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cTrue (.lam A body) arg ha)
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cTrue A value body ha)
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (bvar_ne_cTrue i ha)
  | .delta _ r ls m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (convStuckR_delta_false r ls m hres htr ha)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ =>
      False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => DerivedIota badEnv X b) hdi ha))
  | .lit _ t _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lit_ne_cTrue t ha)
  | .app _ f _ x _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cTrue f x ha)
  | .lam _ A _ body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lam_ne_cTrue A body ha)
  | .pi _ A _ B _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (pi_ne_cTrue A B ha)
  | .letE _ A _ v _ body _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cTrue A v body ha)
  | .sorts _ l _ _ => False.elim (sort_ne_cTrue l ha)
  | .consts _ r ls ls' _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (consts_cTrue_ne_cN r ls ls' ha hb)
  | .eta _ f A _ _ =>
      False.elim (lam_ne_cTrue A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)) ha)
  | .irr _ P _ _ _ hp hq =>
      ConvNT.sortGap (tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common P
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hq hb)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hp ha))
termination_by sizeOf h
end

def convStuckR {a T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a cN T) (ha : a = cTrue) : ConvNT :=
  convStuckAtTrue h ha rfl

def convT_cN_cTrue_stuck {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue T) : ConvNT :=
  convStuck h rfl rfl

/- TyConvT from N to True is either one stuck ConvT, or a split whose
   two halves are not equalities. Reflexive halves are dropped by
   `tyConvT_step`. Not the negation. -/
inductive TyStuck : Type where
  | conv (h : ConvNT) : TyStuck
  | trans (mid : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN mid)
      (h2 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid cTrue) : TyStuck

def tyConvT_cN_stuck {a b : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] a b) (ha : a = cN) (hb : b = cTrue) : TyStuck :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      TyStuck.conv (convStuck hc ha hb)
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyConvT_step h1 with
      | PSum.inl heq => tyConvT_cN_stuck h2 (Eq.trans (Eq.symm heq) ha) hb
      | PSum.inr _ =>
          match tyConvT_step h2 with
          | PSum.inl heq => tyConvT_cN_stuck h1 ha (Eq.trans heq hb)
          | PSum.inr _ =>
              TyStuck.trans mid
                (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => TyConvT badEnv 0 [] X mid) h1 ha)
                (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid X) h2 hb)
termination_by sizeOf h

def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_stuck (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) : TyStuck :=
  tyConvT_cN_stuck h rfl rfl

/- The empty context stores no let value. -/
theorem lookupValue_nil (i : Nat) : lookupValue ([] : LCtx) i = none := rfl

/- `badEnv` above member 15 is `ctlEnv`, and `ctlEnv` stops at 14.
   `16 + n` does not reduce in either match, so the proof splits.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem badEnv_members_ge16 (n : Nat) : badEnv.members (16 + n) = none := by
  have hm : badEnv.members (16 + n) =
      (match (16 + n) with
        | 15 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩
        | r => ctlEnv.members r) := rfl
  rw [hm]
  split
  · next h =>
      exact absurd (h ▸ Nat.le_add_right 16 n) (Nat.not_le_of_gt (by decide))
  · have hc : ctlEnv.members (16 + n) =
        (match (16 + n) with
          | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩
          | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩
          | 4 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
          | 5 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩
          | 6 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 7 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
          | 8 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
          | 9 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 10 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩
          | 11 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩
          | 12 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
              some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩
          | 13 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩
          | 14 => some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩
          | _ => none) := rfl
    rw [hc]
    split <;> first
      | rfl
      | next h =>
          exact absurd (h ▸ Nat.le_add_right 16 n) (Nat.not_le_of_gt (by decide))

/- No member of badEnv is a recursor, so derived ι does not apply.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem badEnv_no_recursor (r : Nat) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hm : badEnv.members r = some m) (hk : m.mclass = .recursorM) : False := by
  match r with
  | 0 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 0 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 1 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 1 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 2 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 2 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 3 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 3 = none := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      cases hm
  | 4 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 4 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 5 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 5 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 6 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 6 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 7 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 7 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 8 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 8 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 9 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 9 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 10 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 10 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 11 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 11 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 12 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 12 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
            some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 13 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 13 = some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 14 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 14 = some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 15 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 15 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | n + 16 =>
      rw [Nat.add_comm] at hm
      rw [badEnv_members_ge16 n] at hm
      cases hm

theorem derivedIota_badEnv_false {lhs rhs : Expr Nat}
    (h : DerivedIota badEnv lhs rhs) : False := by
  cases h with
  | of w => exact badEnv_no_recursor w.recRef w.recMember w.hrec w.hrecK

/- The three transparent bodies, after any level substitution. None is a
   sort. Members 11, 12, and 15 are the only transparent ones. -/
theorem badEnv_tb_11 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 11 ls = some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_12 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 12 ls =
      some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_15 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 15 ls = some cZero := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_none_0 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 0 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_1 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 1 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_2 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 2 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_3 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 3 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_4 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 4 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_5 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 5 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_6 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 6 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_7 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 7 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_8 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 8 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_9 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 9 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_10 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 10 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_13 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 13 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_14 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 14 ls = none := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_none_tail (n : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv (n + 16) ls = none := by
  rw [Nat.add_comm]
  unfold transparentBody
  rw [badEnv_members_ge16 n]

/- `succ (succ zero)` is stuck: `succ` is a constructor. -/
theorem whnf_two_stuck (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) =
      some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) := rfl

theorem whnf_addTwo_body (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) =
      some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) := rfl

theorem whnf_cZero_self (k : Nat) : whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) cZero = some cZero := rfl

/- No constant of badEnv weak-heads to a sort. A rigid head is itself.
   The three transparent bodies are an application of `succ`, a λ, and
   `zero`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem whnf_badEnv_const_not_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level) (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv k (.const r ls) ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  induction k generalizing r ls with
  | zero =>
      intro h
      exact whnf_zero_none h
  | succ k ih =>
      intro h
      match r with
      | 11 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 11 ls _ (badEnv_tb_11 ls)] at h
          cases k with
          | zero => exact whnf_zero_none h
          | succ k =>
              rw [whnf_two_stuck k] at h
              injection h with he
              cases he
      | 12 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 12 ls _ (badEnv_tb_12 ls)] at h
          cases k with
          | zero => exact whnf_zero_none h
          | succ k =>
              rw [whnf_addTwo_body k] at h
              injection h with he
              cases he
      | 15 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 15 ls _ (badEnv_tb_15 ls)] at h
          exact ih 1 [] h
      | 0 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 0 ls (badEnv_tb_none_0 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 1 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 1 ls (badEnv_tb_none_1 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 2 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 2 ls (badEnv_tb_none_2 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 3 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 3 ls (badEnv_tb_none_3 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 4 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 4 ls (badEnv_tb_none_4 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 5 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 5 ls (badEnv_tb_none_5 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 6 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 6 ls (badEnv_tb_none_6 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 7 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 7 ls (badEnv_tb_none_7 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 8 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 8 ls (badEnv_tb_none_8 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 9 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 9 ls (badEnv_tb_none_9 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 10 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 10 ls (badEnv_tb_none_10 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 13 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 13 ls (badEnv_tb_none_13 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 14 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 14 ls (badEnv_tb_none_14 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | n + 16 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k (n + 16) ls (badEnv_tb_none_tail n ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he

theorem whnf_natExpand_zero (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (natExpand 0) = some (natExpand 0) := rfl

theorem whnf_natExpand_succ (t k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (natExpand (t + 1)) = some (natExpand (t + 1)) := rfl

theorem whnf_natExpand_not_sort (t : Nat) (l : Level) (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv k (natExpand t) ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  cases k with
  | zero =>
      intro h
      exact whnf_zero_none h
  | succ k =>
      cases t with
      | zero =>
          intro h
          rw [whnf_natExpand_zero k] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | succ t =>
          intro h
          rw [whnf_natExpand_succ t k] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he

/- A weak-head sort. Fuel is existential, so one successful step is enough.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def IsSort (e : Expr Nat) (l : Level) : Prop :=
  ∃ k, whnfFuel badEnv k e = some (.sort l)

theorem isSort_sort (l : Level) : IsSort (.sort l) l :=
  ⟨1, whnf_sort_self badEnv 0 l⟩

theorem not_isSort_lam (A b : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.lam A b) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_lam_self badEnv k A b] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_pi (A B : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.pi A B) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_pi_self badEnv k A B] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_bvar (i : Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.bvar i) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_bvar_self badEnv k i] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_lit (t : Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.lit t) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_lit_self badEnv k t] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_const (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.const r ls) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  exact whnf_badEnv_const_not_sort r ls l k hk

/- The level `whnfFuel` returns for a sort is that sort's level. -/
theorem isSort_sort_eq (l l' : Level) (h : IsSort (.sort l) l') : eqN l l' := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_sort_self badEnv k l] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he
      exact eqN_refl l

/- One β step moves a sort witness onto the instantiated body. -/
theorem isSort_beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.app (.lam A body) arg) l) : IsSort (instantiate0 arg body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_beta badEnv k A body arg] at hk
      exact ⟨k, hk⟩

theorem isSort_of_beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (instantiate0 arg body) l) : IsSort (.app (.lam A body) arg) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  refine ⟨k + 1, ?_⟩
  rw [whnf_beta badEnv k A body arg]
  exact hk

/- One ζ step moves a sort witness onto the instantiated body. -/
theorem isSort_zeta (A v body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.letE A v body) l) : IsSort (instantiate0 v body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_zeta badEnv k A v body] at hk
      exact ⟨k, hk⟩

theorem isSort_of_zeta (A v body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (instantiate0 v body) l) : IsSort (.letE A v body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  refine ⟨k + 1, ?_⟩
  rw [whnf_zeta badEnv k A v body]
  exact hk

/- Substituting under a lifted term does nothing: the lift pushed every
   index past `j`. No `omega`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem instantiate_lift_cancel (j : Nat) (s e : Expr Nat) :
    instantiate j s (lift j 1 e) = e := by
  induction e generalizing j s with
  | bvar i =>
      by_cases hle : j ≤ i
      · have hlift : lift j 1 (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + 1)) := by
          simp only [lift, if_pos hle]
        rw [hlift]
        have hne : i + 1 ≠ j := by
          intro heq
          exact Nat.not_succ_le_self i (Nat.le_trans (Nat.le_of_eq heq) hle)
        have hlt : j < i + 1 := Nat.lt_succ_of_le hle
        have hinst : instantiate j s (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + 1)) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) ((i + 1) - 1)) := by
          simp only [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
        rw [hinst, Nat.add_sub_cancel i 1]
      · have hlift : lift j 1 (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) := by
          simp only [lift, if_neg hle]
        rw [hlift]
        have hne : i ≠ j := by
          intro heq
          exact hle (Nat.le_of_eq heq.symm)
        have hnlt : ¬ j < i := fun hlt => hle (Nat.le_of_lt hlt)
        simp only [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt]
  | sort _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl
  | app f x ihf ihx =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [ihf j s, ihx j s]
  | lam a b iha ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]
  | pi a b iha ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]
  | letE a v b iha ihv ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihv j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]

/- One `whnfFuel` step on `badEnv`. `none` means the head is already
   weak-head (a sort, a rigid constant, a lambda with no argument, …).
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def spineStep (e : Expr Nat) : Option (Expr Nat) :=
  match appsSpine e with
  | (.lam _ b, arg :: args) => some (foldApps (instantiate0 arg b) args)
  | (.letE _ v b, args) => some (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args)
  | (.const r ls, args) =>
      match transparentBody badEnv r ls with
      | some body => some (foldApps body args)
      | none => none
  | _ => none

theorem whnf_succ (k : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) e =
      (spineStep e).elim (some e) (whnfFuel badEnv k) := by
  match h : appsSpine e with
  | (.lam _ b, arg :: args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.lam _ b, []) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.letE _ v b, args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.const r ls, args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
      split <;> rfl
  | (.bvar _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.sort _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.pi _ _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.lit _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.app _ _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]

/- A sort witness is either the sort itself or one step closer to it.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem isSort_progress (e : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort e l) :
    e = .sort l ∨ ∃ e', spineStep e = some e' ∧ IsSort e' l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_succ k e] at hk
      cases hs : spineStep e with
      | none =>
          simp only [hs, Option.elim] at hk
          injection hk with he
          exact Or.inl he
      | some e' =>
          simp only [hs, Option.elim] at hk
          exact Or.inr ⟨e', rfl, ⟨k, hk⟩⟩

/- A conversion whose left end is already a syntactic sort. `refl` and
   `sorts` keep a sort on the right. `symm`, `trans`, and `irr` do not:
   symmetry of β sends a sort to an application. Not level preservation,
   not `¬ TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp,
   or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvFromSort (l : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvFromSort l (.sort l)
  | symm (a T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a (.sort l) T) :
      ConvFromSort l a
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) m T)
      (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvFromSort l b
  | sorts (l₂ : Level) (h : eqN l l₂) : ConvFromSort l (.sort l₂)
  | irr (b P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvFromSort l b

def convFromSort {b T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) b T) : ConvFromSort l b :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvFromSort.refl
  | .symm _ a _ _ hinner => ConvFromSort.symm a T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvFromSort.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convFromSort hsub
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .sorts _ _ l₂ heq => ConvFromSort.sorts l₂ heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvFromSort.irr b P hP hp hq
termination_by sizeOf h

/- `Sort l₁ = Sort l₂` is `eqN`. Injection on the sort constructor,
   then reflexivity. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem eqN_of_sort_eq {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : (.sort l₁ : Expr Nat) = .sort l₂) : eqN l₁ l₂ :=
  match h with
  | rfl => eqN_refl l₁

/- What remains of a conversion between two syntactic sorts after
   `refl`, `sorts`, symmetry, and `tyConv` are consumed. `trans` keeps
   a middle that is not a sort. `irr` keeps the common proposition.
   `swap` is symmetry of a stuck derivation. The end equalities stay
   hypotheses: rewriting them under the subderivation is what the
   matcher does not do. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvSortStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | trans {l₁ l₂ : Level} {a b : Expr Nat} (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T)
      (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | irr {l₁ l₂ : Level} {p q : Expr Nat} (P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
      (hp_eq : p = .sort l₁) (hq_eq : q = .sort l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | swap {l₁ l₂ : Level} (s : ConvSortStuck l₂ l₁) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | after {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l')
      (s : ConvSortStuck l' l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | before {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l' l₂)
      (s : ConvSortStuck l₁ l') : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂

/- The left half of a `ConvT` from a sort to an unknown middle.
   `refl` and `sorts` make the middle a sort. `other` does not refine
   it, so the right half still starts at that middle. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvLeft (l₁ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvLeft l₁ (.sort l₁)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l') : ConvLeft l₁ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : ConvLeft l₁ mid

/- A nested `trans` whose left half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed.
   `symm` and `irr` do not make the right end a sort. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convLeftAt {l₁ : Level} {mid T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid T) : ConvLeft l₁ mid :=
  match h1 with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvLeft.refl
  | .symm _ a _ _ _ => ConvLeft.other a
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ hA hB =>
      match convLeftAt hA with
      | .refl => convLeftAt hB
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match convLeftAt hB with
          | .refl => ConvLeft.sorts l' heq
          | .sorts l'' heq2 => ConvLeft.sorts l'' (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | .other _ => ConvLeft.other mid
      | .other _ => ConvLeft.other mid
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convLeftAt hsub
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .sorts _ _ l' heq => ConvLeft.sorts l' heq
  | .irr _ _ _ b _ _ _ => ConvLeft.other b
termination_by sizeOf h1

def convLeft {l₁ : Level} {a mid T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a mid T) (ha : a = .sort l₁) : ConvLeft l₁ mid :=
  convLeftAt (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X mid T) h1 ha)

/- What remains of a type conversion between two syntactic sorts.
   `step` is one stuck `ConvT`. `trans` is a split whose left half is
   not a reflexive or `sorts` prefix. `after` carries `eqN` across a
   `sorts` step whose continuation is stuck. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive TySortStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | step {l₁ l₂ : Level} (s : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂
  | trans {l₁ l₂ : Level} {mid : Expr Nat}
      (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid)
      (h2 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid (.sort l₂)) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂
  | after {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l')
      (s : TySortStuck l' l₂) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂

/- The left half of a `TyConvT` between a sort and an unknown middle.
   `refl` and `sorts` make the middle a sort. `other` does not refine
   it, so the two halves still share that middle. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive TyLeft (l₁ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : TyLeft l₁ (.sort l₁)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l') : TyLeft l₁ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : TyLeft l₁ mid

/- A nested `trans` whose left half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed.
   The `of` arm uses `convLeftAt`, so a sort prefix under `ConvT.trans`
   is consumed there too. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def tyLeft {l₁ : Level} {mid : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid) : TyLeft l₁ mid :=
  match h1 with
  | .refl _ _ => TyLeft.refl
  | .of _ _ _ _ hc =>
      match convLeftAt hc with
      | .refl => TyLeft.refl
      | .sorts l' heq => TyLeft.sorts l' heq
      | .other a => TyLeft.other a
  | .trans _ _ m _ hA hB =>
      match tyLeft hA with
      | .refl => tyLeft hB
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match tyLeft hB with
          | .refl => TyLeft.sorts l' heq
          | .sorts l'' heq2 => TyLeft.sorts l'' (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | .other _ => TyLeft.other mid
      | .other _ => TyLeft.other mid
termination_by sizeOf h1

/- `succ` on levels is injective for `eqN`. The evaluator adds one, and
   `Nat.succ` is injective. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem eqN_succ_inj {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN (.succ l₁) (.succ l₂)) : eqN l₁ l₂ := by
  intro ρ
  have hρ : Rsx.eval ρ (.succ l₁) = Rsx.eval ρ (.succ l₂) := h ρ
  simp only [Rsx.eval] at hρ
  cases h₁ : Rsx.eval ρ l₁ with
  | none =>
      cases h₂ : Rsx.eval ρ l₂ with
      | none => rfl
      | some n =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          cases hρ
  | some n =>
      cases h₂ : Rsx.eval ρ l₂ with
      | none =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          cases hρ
      | some m =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          injection hρ with hnm
          injection hnm with hn
          subst hn
          rfl

/- `instantiate index arg body` is a sort only when the body is that sort,
   or the body is the substituted variable and the argument is that sort.
   An application, lambda, product, let, literal, or constant stays that
   constructor. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem instantiate_eq_sort (index : Nat) (arg body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiate index arg body = .sort l) :
    body = .sort l ∨ (body = .bvar index ∧ arg = .sort l) := by
  cases body with
  | sort l' =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
      exact Or.inl rfl
  | bvar i =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      by_cases heq : i = index
      · simp only [heq, if_pos rfl] at h
        exact Or.inr ⟨by subst heq; rfl, h⟩
      · simp only [if_neg heq] at h
        by_cases hlt : index < i
        · simp only [if_pos hlt] at h
          cases h
        · simp only [if_neg hlt] at h
          cases h
  | const _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | app _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | lam _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | pi _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | letE _ _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | lit _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h

theorem instantiate0_eq_sort (arg body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiate0 arg body = .sort l) :
    body = .sort l ∨ (body = .bvar 0 ∧ arg = .sort l) :=
  instantiate_eq_sort 0 arg body l h

/- A `badEnv` transparent body, after level substitution, is never a sort.
   The only transparent members are 11, 12, and 15, and each body is an
   application, a lambda, or `zero`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem transparentBody_badEnv_ne_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv r ls ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  intro h
  match r with
  | 0 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_0] at h
      cases h
  | 1 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_1] at h
      cases h
  | 2 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_2] at h
      cases h
  | 3 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_3] at h
      cases h
  | 4 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_4] at h
      cases h
  | 5 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_5] at h
      cases h
  | 6 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_6] at h
      cases h
  | 7 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_7] at h
      cases h
  | 8 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_8] at h
      cases h
  | 9 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_9] at h
      cases h
  | 10 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_10] at h
      cases h
  | 11 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_11] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | 12 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_12] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | 13 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_13] at h
      cases h
  | 14 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_14] at h
      cases h
  | 15 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_15] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | n + 16 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_tail n] at h
      cases h

theorem badEnv_delta_rhs_ne_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (b : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (hbody : m.body = some b)
    (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls b = .sort l) : False := by
  apply transparentBody_badEnv_ne_sort r ls l
  unfold transparentBody
  rw [hres]
  dsimp
  rw [htr, hbody]
  dsimp
  change some (instantiateLevels ls b) = some (.sort l)
  rw [h]

/- The empty context stores no let value, so `zetaLocal` has no witness. -/
theorem lookup_nil_no_value (i : Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : lookupValue ([] : LCtx) i = some v) : False := by
  rw [lookupValue_nil] at h
  cases h

/- A literal expands to `succ^n zero`, never a sort. -/
theorem lit_expand_ne_sort (t : Nat) (exp : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : LiteralExpansion t exp) (hs : exp = .sort l) : False := by
  cases h
  exact natExpand_ne_sort t l hs

/- A conversion whose right end is a syntactic sort. The equality is a
   hypothesis, so `beta` and `zeta` stay in the match: their contractum
   is a sort only when `instantiate0_eq_sort` says so, and that `Or` is
   not eliminated here. Delta, literal expansion, and `zetaLocal` in the
   empty context are impossible. A rigid non-sort right head contradicts
   the equality. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or
   AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvToSort (l : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvToSort l (.sort l)
  | symm (a b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l b
  | trans (m c a T : Expr Nat) (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T)
      (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m c T) (hc : c = .sort l) : ConvToSort l a
  | sorts (l₁ : Level) (h : eqN l₁ l) : ConvToSort l (.sort l₁)
  | beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (hr : instantiate0 arg body = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.app (.lam A body) arg)
  | zeta (A value body : Expr Nat) (hr : instantiate0 value body = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.letE A value body)
  | eta (f A B : Expr Nat) (h : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] f (.pi A B)) (hf : f = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.lam A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)))
  | irr (p q P : Expr Nat) (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
      (hq_eq : q = .sort l) : ConvToSort l p

def convToSort {a b T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (hs : b = .sort l) : ConvToSort l a :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ =>
      Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvToSort l X)
        (ConvToSort.refl (l := l)) (Eq.symm hs)
  | .symm _ x y _ hinner => ConvToSort.symm x y T hinner hs
  | .trans _ x m c _ h1 h2 =>
      let other := ConvToSort.trans m c x T h1 h2 hs
      match convToSort h2 hs with
      | .refl => convToSort h1 rfl
      | _ => other
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convToSort hsub hs
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => ConvToSort.beta A body arg hs
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => ConvToSort.zeta A value body hs
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ hval _ _ => False.elim (lookup_nil_no_value i hval)
  | .delta _ r ls m body hres hbody htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_delta_rhs_ne_sort r ls m body l hres hbody htr hs)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .lit _ t exp _ hexp _ => False.elim (lit_expand_ne_sort t exp l hexp hs)
  | .app _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .lam _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .pi _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .letE _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .sorts _ l₁ _ heq =>
      ConvToSort.sorts l₁ (eqN_trans heq (eqN_of_sort_eq hs))
  | .consts _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .eta _ f A B h => ConvToSort.eta f A B h hs
  | .irr _ P p q hP hp hq => ConvToSort.irr p q P hP hp hq hs
termination_by sizeOf h

/- What the right end's inversion says about the left end.
   `refl` and `sorts` make that end a sort. `other` does not.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvRight (l₂ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvRight l₂ (.sort l₂)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l' l₂) : ConvRight l₂ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : ConvRight l₂ mid

/- Read a top-level `symm` with `convLeft`. Beta, zeta, eta, and irr
   stay `other`: those left heads are an application, a let, a lambda,
   or an unexamined proof. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convRightOf {l₂ : Level} {m : Expr Nat}
    (v : ConvToSort l₂ m) : ConvRight l₂ m :=
  match v with
  | .refl => ConvRight.refl
  | .sorts l' heq => ConvRight.sorts l' heq
  | .symm _ b _ hinner hx =>
      match convLeft hinner hx with
      | .refl => ConvRight.refl
      | .sorts l' heq => ConvRight.sorts l' (eqN_symm heq)
      | .other _ => ConvRight.other b
  | .trans _ _ a _ _ _ _ => ConvRight.other a
  | .beta A body arg _ => ConvRight.other (.app (.lam A body) arg)
  | .zeta A value body _ => ConvRight.other (.letE A value body)
  | .eta f A _ _ _ => ConvRight.other (.lam A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)))
  | .irr p _ _ _ _ _ _ => ConvRight.other p

def convRight {m b T : Expr Nat} {l₂ : Level}
    (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) (hb : b = .sort l₂) : ConvRight l₂ m :=
  convRightOf (convToSort h2 hb)

/- Both ends are sorts by separate equalities. A `trans` whose left
   half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed. If the left half is `other`,
   the right half is read by `convRight`: a sort middle recurses on
   the left piece. Beta, zeta, eta, and irr on the right stay
   `ConvSortStuck.trans`. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def convBothSort {a b T : Expr Nat} {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ =>
      PSum.inl (eqN_of_sort_eq (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner =>
      match convBothSort hinner hb ha with
      | PSum.inl heq => PSum.inl (eqN_symm heq)
      | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.swap s)
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      match convLeft h1 ha with
      | .refl => convBothSort h2 rfl hb
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match convBothSort h2 rfl hb with
          | PSum.inl heq2 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.after l' heq s)
      | .other _ =>
          let stuck := PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.trans m T h1 h2 ha hb)
          match convRight h2 hb with
          | .refl => convBothSort h1 ha rfl
          | .sorts l' heq =>
              match convBothSort h1 ha rfl with
              | PSum.inl heq1 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq1 heq)
              | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.before l' heq s)
          | .other _ => stuck
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convBothSort hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .zeta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .zetaLocal _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .delta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .lit _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .app _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .lam _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .pi _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .letE _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .sorts _ _ _ heq =>
      PSum.inl (eqN_trans (eqN_symm (eqN_of_sort_eq ha))
        (eqN_trans heq (eqN_of_sort_eq hb)))
  | .consts _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .eta _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq =>
      PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.irr P hP hp hq ha hb)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- The right half of a sort-to-sort `trans`, packaged as one `ConvT`.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convTransRight {l₁ l₂ : Level} {a b m T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T)
    (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  convBothSort (ConvT.trans [] a m b T h1 h2) ha hb

/- `TyConvT` between two sorts. A reflexive left half is dropped. A
   `sorts` left half composes `eqN`. Anything else is `TySortStuck`.
   Not `¬ TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue`. -/
def tyBothSort {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) (.sort l₂)) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (TySortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => PSum.inl (eqN_refl l₁)
  | .of _ _ _ _ hc =>
      match convBothSort hc rfl rfl with
      | PSum.inl heq => PSum.inl heq
      | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.step s)
  | .trans _ _ _ _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyLeft h1 with
      | .refl => tyBothSort h2
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match tyBothSort h2 with
          | PSum.inl heq2 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.after l' heq s)
      | .other _ => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.trans h1 h2)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are not `eqN`. A derivation of that `TyConvT`
   is therefore a stuck `trans` or `irr`, not a level equality. Not
   `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def sortGap_stuck
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero)) :
    TySortStuck (.succ .zero) .zero :=
  match tyBothSort h with
  | PSum.inl heq => False.elim (eqN_succ_ne_zero .zero heq)
  | PSum.inr s => s

/- Proof irrelevance of two syntactic sorts. Their principal universes
   are `Sort (succ l₁)` and `Sort (succ l₂)`. Those are `eqN`, and then
   `succ` is injective, or the type conversion between them is stuck.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvIrrStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | principal {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l₁' l₂' : Level)
      (heq1 : eqN l₁' (.succ l₁)) (heq2 : eqN l₂' (.succ l₂))
      (s : TySortStuck l₁' l₂') : ConvIrrStuck l₁ l₂

def convIrrPrincipal {l₁ l₂ : Level} {p q P : Expr Nat}
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
    (hp_eq : p = .sort l₁) (hq_eq : q = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvIrrStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match hasTyT_sort_principal hp hp_eq with
  | ⟨l₁', ⟨heq1, ht1⟩⟩ =>
      match hasTyT_sort_principal hq hq_eq with
      | ⟨l₂', ⟨heq2, ht2⟩⟩ =>
          match tyBothSort (tyConvT_of_to_same ht1 ht2) with
          | PSum.inl heq =>
              PSum.inl (eqN_succ_inj
                (eqN_trans (eqN_symm heq1) (eqN_trans heq heq2)))
          | PSum.inr s =>
              PSum.inr (ConvIrrStuck.principal l₁' l₂' heq1 heq2 s)

/- `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are not `eqN`, so proof irrelevance of those
   two sorts is a stuck conversion of their principal universes.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convIrrSuccZero {p q P : Expr Nat}
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
    (hp_eq : p = .sort (.succ .zero)) (hq_eq : q = .sort .zero) :
    ConvIrrStuck (.succ .zero) .zero :=
  match convIrrPrincipal hp hq hp_eq hq_eq with
  | PSum.inl heq => False.elim (eqN_succ_ne_zero .zero heq)
  | PSum.inr s => s

theorem cBadData : DataTy badEnv (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  ⟨4, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cBadNorm : norm badEnv 3 cBad = some cZero := rfl
theorem cBadVal : scmValOf badEnv 1 cZero = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem cBadRel : relevantSpine badEnv 0 1 cZero = true := rfl
theorem cBadRoot : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cZero = false := by decide
theorem cBadFits : valFits 1 tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem cBad_irrelevant : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cBad = true := by decide

/-- the reference lowering of `c` is the refusing term at every fuel and type. -/
theorem lowerF_cBad {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF badEnv 0 F (S := S) t cBad = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] (.const 15 []) = true := cBad_irrelevant
    have he : erase badEnv 0 (F + 1) [] cBad = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, cBad, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- the counterexample: the reference family does not meet the session-7 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_untypedEnv {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementUntypedEnv (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h badEnv 0 3 1 cBad _ cZero tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list []))
    cBadTy cBadData cBadNorm cBadVal cBadRel cBadRoot cBadFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF badEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) tyNat1 cBad) = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_cBad] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- the same witness as a gap guard: data on the value side, refused by the lowering, the
-- unfolded value relevant while the constant is a proof, and the body typed by the
-- certified checker at `N`, not at the declared `True`
#guard (obs badEnv cBad).isSome && (runLowered (Rsx.lower badEnv (t := tyNat1) cBad)).isNone &&
  irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cBad && !(irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cZero) &&
  decide (inferT badEnv 0 [] cZero = some cN) && decide (inferT badEnv 0 [] cZero ≠ some cTrue)
-- a well-typed body of the same shape (`c : N := zero`, member 11-like) is lowered: `g06`
#guard agrees (fun t e => Rsx.lower badEnv (t := t) e) badEnv tyNat3 g06

/-! ### Counterexamples to the session-8 statement: the relevance test is syntactic

`Rsx.irrelevant` reads the certified syntactic checker `inferT` (no conversion rule), and
`isPropSort` matches `Sort 0` as written. `lvlEnv` (members 0…5):
0 `I : Sort (max 0 0)` (an inductive in a sort equal to `Prop`, `eqN`), 1 `K : I`,
2 `IdP : Sort (max 0 0) → Sort 0 := fun A => A`, 3 `c : IdP I := K`, 4 `J : Type`,
5 `Mk : IdP I → J`. Every body is typed at its declared type (`lvlBodiesTyped`, through
`ConvT.sorts`, `.pi`, `.delta`, `.beta`).

1. `c` is typed at `I` only through conversion (`IdP I ≡ I`); `I` is an inductive, so `DataTy`
   holds; `norm` unfolds `c` to `K`. Erasure tests `c`: its declared type `IdP I` has
   syntactic type `Sort 0`, so `c ↦ □` and the lowering refuses. The value `K` has type `I`,
   whose syntactic type is `Sort (max 0 0)`, not `Sort 0` as written: relevant.
2. `Mk c` is syntactically typed at `J`. Erasure keeps `Mk` and erases the field `c`;
   `norm` gives `Mk K`, whose field `K` passes `relevantSpine`; evalLF of the lowering returns
   `.inj 5 (.list [])`, the value side `.inj 5 (.list [.inj 1 (.list [])])`.

The statement on main requires `inferT E n [] e = some T` and `(inferT E n [] v).isSome`;
witness 1 has `inferT c = IdP I` (not a data type) and witness 2 has `inferT (Mk K) = none`
(`IdP I` vs `I` as written): `convTyped_witness_excluded`, `convValue_witness_excluded`. -/

def lvl00 : Level := .max .zero .zero

theorem lvl00_eqN : eqN lvl00 .zero := fun _ => rfl

def wI : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def wK : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def wId : Expr Nat := .const 2 []
def wC : Expr Nat := .const 3 []
def wJ : Expr Nat := .const 4 []
def wMk : Expr Nat := .const 5 []
def wIdBody : Expr Nat := .lam (.sort lvl00) (.bvar 0)

def mI : CheckedMember := ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort lvl00, none⟩
def mK : CheckedMember := ⟨.constructorM, 0, wI, none⟩
def mId : CheckedMember := ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero), some wIdBody⟩
def mC : CheckedMember := ⟨.definitionM, 0, .app wId wI, some wK⟩
def mJ : CheckedMember := ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
def mMk : CheckedMember := ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi (.app wId wI) wJ, none⟩

def lvlEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some mI
    | 1 => some mK
    | 2 => some mId
    | 3 => some mC
    | 4 => some mJ
    | 5 => some mMk
    | _ => none

def wSortTy (Γ : LCtx) : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 Γ (.sort lvl00) (.sort (.succ lvl00)) := .sort Γ lvl00

/-- `Sort (max 0 0) ≡ Sort 0` (`ConvT.sorts`, levels extensionally equal). -/
def wSortConv (Γ : LCtx) : ConvT lvlEnv 0 Γ (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.sort (.succ lvl00)) :=
  .sorts Γ lvl00 .zero lvl00_eqN

def wITy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wI (.sort lvl00) := .const [] 0 [] mI rfl rfl rfl
def wKTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wK wI := .const [] 1 [] mK rfl rfl rfl

def wVar0 : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [.assumption (.sort lvl00)] (.bvar 0) (.sort lvl00) :=
  .bvar [.assumption (.sort lvl00)] 0 (.sort lvl00) rfl

def wIdBodyTy0 : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00)) :=
  .lam [] (.sort lvl00) (.succ lvl00) (.bvar 0) (.sort lvl00) (wSortTy []) wVar0

def wPiConv : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00)) (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero))
    (.sort (.imax (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00))) :=
  .pi [] (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00)
    (.refl [] (.sort lvl00) _ (wSortTy [])) (wSortConv _)

def wIdBodyTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero)) :=
  .conv [] wIdBody _ _ (.imax (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00)) wIdBodyTy0 wPiConv

def wIdDelta : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] wId wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero)) :=
  .delta [] 2 [] mId wIdBody rfl rfl rfl rfl rfl wIdBodyTy

def wAppConv : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wId wI) (.app wIdBody wI) (.sort .zero) :=
  .app [] wId wIdBody wI wI (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) wIdDelta (.refl [] wI _ wITy)

def wBeta : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wIdBody wI) wI (.sort lvl00) :=
  .beta [] (.sort lvl00) (.bvar 0) wI (.sort lvl00) (.succ lvl00) (wSortTy []) wVar0 wITy

def wBeta0 : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wIdBody wI) wI (.sort .zero) :=
  .tyConv [] _ _ (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.succ lvl00) wBeta (wSortConv [])

/-- `IdP I ≡ I : Sort 0`. -/
def wIdI : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wId wI) wI (.sort .zero) :=
  .trans [] _ _ _ _ wAppConv wBeta0

def wCBodyTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wK (.app wId wI) :=
  .conv [] wK wI (.app wId wI) .zero wKTy (.symm [] _ _ _ wIdI)

/-- witness 1's typing: `c : I`, through conversion only. -/
def wCTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wC wI :=
  .conv [] wC (.app wId wI) wI .zero (.const [] 3 [] mC rfl rfl rfl) wIdI

/-- every transparent body of `lvlEnv` is typed at its declared type. -/
theorem lvlBodiesTyped : BodiesTyped lvlEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm ht hb hlen _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 2, hm =>
    cases hm; cases hb
    cases ls with
    | nil => exact ⟨wIdBodyTy⟩
    | cons _ _ => exact absurd hlen (Nat.succ_ne_zero _)
  | 3, hm =>
    cases hm; cases hb
    cases ls with
    | nil => exact ⟨wCBodyTy⟩
    | cons _ _ => exact absurd hlen (Nat.succ_ne_zero _)
  | 4, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 5, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | _ + 6, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem wIData : DataTy lvlEnv wI := ⟨0, [], [], mI, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
theorem wCNorm : norm lvlEnv 3 wC = some wK := rfl
theorem wKVal : scmValOf lvlEnv 1 wK = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem wKRel : relevantSpine lvlEnv 0 1 wK = true := rfl
theorem wKRoot : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wK = false := by decide
theorem wKFits : valFits 1 tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem wC_irrelevant : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wC = true := by decide

theorem lowerF_wC {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF lvlEnv 0 F (S := S) t wC = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 3 []) = true := wC_irrelevant
    have he : erase lvlEnv 0 (F + 1) [] wC = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, wC, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- witness 1: the reference family does not meet the session-8 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_convTyped {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementConvTyped (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h lvlEnv 0 3 1 wC _ wK tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) lvlBodiesTyped
    wCTy wIData wCNorm wKVal wKRel wKRoot wKFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) tyNat1 wC) = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_wC] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

/-- witness 1 is outside the statement on main: the checker types `c` at `IdP I`, which is
    not a data type (its head `IdP` is a definition). -/
theorem convTyped_witness_excluded (T : Expr Nat) (h : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some T) :
    ¬ DataTy lvlEnv T := by
  have h1 : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some (.app wId wI) := by decide
  rw [h1] at h
  cases h
  intro ⟨r, ls, args, m, hs, hm, hc⟩
  have hs0 : appsSpine (.app wId wI) = (.const 2 [], [wI]) := rfl
  rw [hs0] at hs
  injection hs with hh _
  injection hh with hr _
  subst hr
  cases hm
  exact absurd hc (by decide)

def wMkC : Expr Nat := .app wMk wC
def wMkK : Expr Nat := .app wMk wK
def tyW2 : BootTy := sumL 6 (sumL 2 .i64)
def wMkVal : Val := .inj 5 (.list [.inj 1 (.list [])])

theorem wMkCInfer : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkC = some wJ := by decide
theorem wJData : DataTy lvlEnv wJ := ⟨4, [], [], mJ, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
theorem wMkCNorm : norm lvlEnv 5 wMkC = some wMkK := rfl
theorem wMkKVal : scmValOf lvlEnv 2 wMkK = some wMkVal := rfl
theorem wMkKRel : relevantSpine lvlEnv 0 2 wMkK = true := by decide
theorem wMkKRoot : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK = false := by decide
theorem wMkKFits : valFits 2 tyW2 wMkVal = true := by decide
theorem wMkCErase (F : Nat) : erase lvlEnv 0 (F + 2) [] wMkC = some (.app (.ctor 5) .box) := by
  have h0 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.app (.const 5 []) (.const 3 [])) = false := by decide
  have h1 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 5 []) = false := by decide
  have h2 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 3 []) = true := wC_irrelevant
  simp only [erase, wMkC, wMk, wC, eraseWith, h0, h1, h2, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, if_true,
    noGlobals]
  rfl

/-- the lowering of `Mk c` from fuel 2 on: the constructor with its erased field dropped. -/
theorem lowerF_wMkC {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) :
    lowerF lvlEnv 0 (F + 2) (S := S) tyW2 wMkC = lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [wMkCErase F, wMkCErase 0]
  rfl

theorem eval_emit_ctor_box {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (m F r : Nat) (ts : List BootTy)
    (τ : BootTy) (hg : ts.get? r = some (.list τ)) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.sum ts) (.ctor r [.box])) = some (.inj r (.list [])) := by
  obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
  simp only [emit, emitWith]
  rw [dif_pos hlt]
  split
  · rename_i τ' hτ'
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
    rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
    simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
  · rename_i hne
    exact absurd hget (hne τ)

theorem eval_lowerF_wMkC {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (m : Nat) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC) = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := by
  have hlow : lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC = emit 2 tyW2 (.ctor 5 [.box]) := by
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [wMkCErase 0]
    rfl
  rw [hlow]
  exact eval_emit_ctor_box progs m 1 5 (List.replicate 6 (.list (sumL 2 .i64))) (sumL 2 .i64) rfl

/-- witness 2: the reference family does not meet the session-8 statement (a wrong value,
    not a refusal). -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_convValue {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementConvTyped (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h lvlEnv 0 5 2 wMkC _ wMkK tyW2 wMkVal lvlBodiesTyped
    (hasTyT_of_inferT wMkCInfer) wJData wMkCNorm wMkKVal wMkKRel wMkKRoot wMkKFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF (F₀ + 2) (Nat.le_add_right _ _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 (F₀ + 2) (S := S) tyW2 wMkC) = some wMkVal := he
  rw [lowerF_wMkC] at he'
  cases lf with
  | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at he'; exact Option.noConfusion he'
  | succ m =>
    rw [eval_lowerF_wMkC] at he'
    have h1 := Option.some.inj he'
    simp only [wMkVal] at h1
    injection h1 with _ h2
    injection h2 with h3
    exact List.noConfusion h3

/-- witness 2 is outside the statement on main: the checker cannot type the value `Mk K`
    (`Mk`'s domain is `IdP I` as written, `K`'s type is `I`). -/
theorem convValue_witness_excluded : (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK).isSome = false := by decide

-- the same witnesses as guards: data on the value side, the lowering refuses (1) or returns
-- another value (2), and the statement's checker premises fail on each
#guard (obs lvlEnv wC).isSome && (runLowered (Rsx.lower lvlEnv (t := tyNat1) wC)).isNone &&
  irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wC && !(irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wK) &&
  decide (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some (.app wId wI))
#guard (obs lvlEnv wMkC).isSome && !(agrees (fun t e => Rsx.lower lvlEnv (t := t) e) lvlEnv tyW2 wMkC)
  && (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkC).isSome && !(inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK).isSome

/-! ### Counterexample to `Rsx.adequacyStatement`: a discarded relevant loop

`whnfFuel` reduces `app (λ_. lit 0) loop` without entering `loop`; `erase` unfolds the
transparent `loop := loop` at every fuel and returns `none`. The value side is `.int 0`.
Cited shape: call-by-name head reduction versus structural erasure (Letouzey, TYPES 2002,
traverses every subterm; Lean's compiled code evaluates a relevant argument). -/

def loopEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 0 [], none⟩
    | 3 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .const 0 [], some (.const 3 [])⟩
    | _ => none

def loopC : Expr Nat := .const 3 []
def bomb : Expr Nat := .app (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) loopC

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem loop_irr : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] loopC = false := by decide

theorem loop_body : transparentBody loopEnv 3 [] = some loopC := rfl

/-- `loop := loop` has no finite erasure: each fuel unfolds it once. -/
theorem erase_loop_none : ∀ F, erase loopEnv 0 F [] loopC = none
  | 0 => rfl
  | F + 1 => by
      simp only [erase, eraseWith, loopC, loop_irr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
        noGlobals, loop_body]
      exact erase_loop_none F

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_irr : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] bomb = false := by decide

theorem erase_bomb_none : ∀ F, erase loopEnv 0 F [] bomb = none
  | 0 => rfl
  | F + 1 => by
      have hirr :
          irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] (.app (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) loopC) = false := by
        simpa [bomb] using bomb_irr
      have hloop :
          eraseWith (irrelevant loopEnv 0) noGlobals loopEnv F [] loopC = none := by
        simpa [erase] using erase_loop_none F
      simp only [erase, eraseWith, bomb, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      rw [hloop]
      -- the app match does not reduce while its first scrutinee is a free
      -- `eraseWith` (Lean's joint matcher). `none` on the argument kills both arms.
      cases eraseWith (irrelevant loopEnv 0) noGlobals loopEnv F []
          (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) <;> rfl

theorem lowerF_bomb {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF loopEnv 0 F (S := S) t bomb = refuse := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [erase_bomb_none F]

theorem bomb_norm : norm loopEnv 3 bomb = some (.lit 0) := rfl
theorem bomb_val : scmValOf loopEnv 1 (.lit 0) = some (.int 0) := rfl
theorem bomb_rel : relevantSpine loopEnv 0 1 (.lit 0) = true := rfl
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_root : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] (.lit 0) = false := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_fits : valFits 1 .i64 (.int 0) = true := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_infer : inferT loopEnv 0 [] bomb = some (.const 0 []) := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_vinfer : (inferT loopEnv 0 [] (.lit 0)).isSome = true := by decide
theorem bomb_data : DataTy loopEnv (.const 0 []) :=
  ⟨0, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem loopBodiesTyped : BodiesTyped loopEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm _ hb hlen hwf
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm
  | 3, hm =>
      cases hm
      cases hb
      cases ls with
      | nil =>
          exact ⟨.const [] 3 [] ⟨.definitionM, 0, .const 0 [], some (.const 3 [])⟩ rfl rfl hwf⟩
      | cons _ _ => exact Nat.noConfusion hlen
  | n + 4, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

/- β of `λ_. c ·`, `c` a rigid constructor, applied to one literal.
   The body mentions only the bound index, so `instantiate0` is that
   application. Letouzey TYPES 2002 keeps a relevant λ; Reynolds 1972 §8
   runs its body in the one-element environment. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_lam_ctor_bvar (c : Nat) (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la) =
      (let q := convWith capRen id [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }] la
       (.apply (.clo 0 []) q.1, q.2)) := rfl

theorem run_lit_any (code : List Code) (F k : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_ctor_any (code : List Code) (F r : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.ctor r) = some (.ctor r []) := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_beta_ctor_body (code : List Code) (F c nlit : Nat) :
    run code (F + 2) [.lit nlit] (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0)) =
      some (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
  rw [run_apply_eq code (F + 1) [.lit nlit] (.ctor c) (.var 0)]
  rw [run_ctor_any code F c [.lit nlit], run_var0 code F [] (.lit nlit)]
  rfl

theorem run_beta_ctor_lit (F c nlit : Nat) :
    run [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }] (F + 3) []
      (.apply (.clo 0 []) (.lit nlit)) = some (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
  refine run_apply_clo_nil
      [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }]
      (F + 1) 0 [] (.lit nlit) (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0))
      (.lit nlit) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) rfl ?_ ?_
  · exact run_lit_any _ (F + 1) nlit []
  · exact run_beta_ctor_body _ F c nlit

theorem norm_beta_ctor_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A : Expr Nat) (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) : Expr Nat) =
      .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := rfl
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2)
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hstuck : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, List.nil_append, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [hbeta, hsub, hstuck]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_beta_ctor_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hbeta : whnfFuel E 1
            (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hbeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_ctor_lit E j c nlit lsc A hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

theorem good_beta_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n []
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_ctor_lit_val E lf c nlit lsc A hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) =>
                    ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have hB : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
                have hC : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) =
                    some (.ctor c) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hBody : erase E n 2 (.assumption A :: [])
                    (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0)) := by
                  rw [erase_app_keep E n 1 (.assumption A :: [])
                    (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0) hirrA]
                  simp only [hC, hB]
                have hLam : erase E n 3 [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) =
                    some (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) := by
                  rw [erase_lam_keep E n 2 [] A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) hirrL]
                  simp only [hBody, Option.map]
                have hLit : erase E n 3 [] (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := rfl
                have he : erase E n 4 []
                    (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  rw [erase_app_keep E n 3 []
                    (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit) hirr]
                  simp only [hLam, hLit]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 4 (S := S) (.sum ts)
                    (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 4 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hE2 := eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 4 (S := S) (.sum ts)
                      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs 1 [] 2 4 (.sum ts)
                    (.ctor c [.lit nlit])
                    (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
                    (Nat.le_add_right 2 2) hE2
                exact ⟨4, 1, hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

theorem lowerF_not_adequate_divArg {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatement (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h loopEnv 0 3 1 bomb (.const 0 []) (.lit 0) .i64 (.int 0)
    loopBodiesTyped bomb_infer bomb_data bomb_norm bomb_val bomb_rel bomb_root bomb_fits bomb_vinfer
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF loopEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) .i64 bomb) = some (.int 0) := he
  rw [lowerF_bomb] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- fuel 4, not `defaultFuel`: `Rsx.lower` is fuel 10000, and each step of `loop`
-- re-enters `inferT`. `lowerF_bomb` already covers every fuel, including that one.
#guard optValEq (obs loopEnv bomb) (some (.int 0)) &&
  (runLowered (lowerF loopEnv 0 4 (t := .i64) bomb)).isNone

end Lower
end Rsx

